{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition","id":411243,"title":"What do you want from a Second Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-19T02:58:39-08:00","id":411243,"title":"What do you want from a Second Edition?","content":"We'll be seeing a Vigil 2e at somepoint, and if as much love goes into the project that we're seeing for Mage and Promethean, then I'll be happy. But what do you want from a revised version of the game?<br /> <br /> I've got two pressing needs. First, I'd love for the game to open up the Vigil to something beyond &quot;kill the monster.&quot; HtV has something as a reputation as the D&amp;D of nWoD, and I feel like a lot could be done to combat that expectation; goce Hunters things to do beyond &quot;investigate until combat,&quot; maybe open up supernatural relations a little, and throw some emphasis on life beyond the hunt. Let Werewolf be the game where your life revolves around the pursuit.<br /> <br /> The other is an overhaul to the organizations. I feel like the core Compacts/Conspiracies list can be shaken up a little (the Knights of St. George deserve a core spot, and I'd love to see more of VASCU), and the existing groups definitely need some love; the Ascending Ones need it the most, but I feel like the Aegis Kai Doru needs a rewrite an awful lot. Define the groups beyond &quot;here's how you kill things, and here's the tools you kill with,&quot; especially in a mundane sense; what does downtime look like for a member of the Lucifuge? Make them feel more like groups to belong to. Give them some history that feels nice and heavy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T10:34:20-08:00","id":412930,"title":"","content":"More ideas beyond the other splats to hunt. The World of Darkness is supposed to be full of mystery, and while it's great being able to link in the other splats as targets, it would be better if we could finally use a splat to explore the rest of the actual World of Darkness, instead of the other gamelines. Especially since first edition had to really reach in order to find reasons to hunt the other gamelines, only one of which is actually purposely detrimental to mankind. It got to the point that by Mortal Remains, changelings were practically babysat by hunters and sin-eaters are allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-20-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:35:53-08:00","id":413128,"title":"","content":"Here's a repost of the stuff I'd like to see with some additions.<br /> <br /> 1) The lack of any real support for actually playing a Tier 2 or Tier 3 story. There's no mechanics for operating at that scale, and far more importantly, there's virtually no fluff explaining how the organisations are... well organised. Adding a new section (or replacing the Hunters section if space is too limited) that gives an outline of each groups organisational structure and their general strategy would be a massive improvement.<br /> <br /> 2) Explicitly setting a theme and mood for each organisation. Sometimes &quot;alone and ignorant against the darkness&quot; suits TF:V, and sometimes they're flying a black helicopter loaded with inferno missiles towards a vampire prince. I get the feeling that there are occasions where TF:V has been forced square-peg-round-hole into &quot;alone and ignorant against the darkness&quot;, it would be better if there was a nice round hole for every organisation.<br /> <br /> 3) A clear separation between Hunters who have and who have not been subverted by monsters. My preferred version will be to present each organisation once with a full write up that portrays them as un-subverted. Then in the antagonists chapter have a paragraph detailing an alternative version of the organisation that is under a monster's sway.<br /> <br /> Note that I don't consider minor templates like Ghouls to be &quot;monsters&quot;. Morally dubious, sure, but still human. I'd also make a special exception for God being in control of the Long Night and the MM; provided that 1) A reasonable interpretation of the books could say that he's not actually in control. 2) A reasonable interpretation of the books could say that it's a good thing for humanity that he is in control. I am ok with additional interpretations on top of this.<br /> <br /> 4) More hunters being awesome. Apart from the Mage orders, Conspiracies are canonically the largest and often the oldest organisations in the WoD. They also seem to have far less infighting than the Pentacle/Inviticus. I want to see that power. The Masqurade exists because of Hunters, let me play the MM when it goes on the warpath outright exterminating continents worth of vampires. Let me command entire TF:V battleships against giant monsters. At the least I'd like one &quot;big gun&quot; Endowment for each Conspiracy that may only be used in special circumstances, a TF:V attack helicopter or a Benediction to smite people with lightning bolts.<br /> <br /> What's the point of having three different Tiers, if you don't have one of those tiers where the average monster quakes in fear of your name and you go toe to toe with entire Freeholds or Scorpion Cults.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing that Hunter could do that isn't in God Machine Core. Religion. I don't know if it's intentional, but here's a list of religious organisations in Hunter: Ahl al-Jabal, Long Night, Ascending Ones, The Faithful of Shulpae, Knights of Saint Adrian, Knights of Saint George, Les Mysteres, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum<br /> <br /> And here's a list of the explicitly Abrahamic religious groups: Ahl al-Jabal, Long Night, Ascending Ones, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum<br /> <br /> Out of twelve official Conspiracies, <b>seven! </b>are explicitly religious. That's the majority. Out of the corebook, three of six are explicitly Abrahamic! Obviously I'm counting the Ascending Ones as 1 rather than 1/3<br /> <br /> I don't want to see region becoming a huge deal, at least not bigger than it is but I think that hunter should support the following kinds of monsters: Abrahamic angels. Abrahamic demons. Egyptian Gods. In short, the monsters with explicit ties to a core 12 org. The best way to do it would probably be creating an equivilent to WoD Inferno (the concept of a template applied to different kids Ephemerial being will work as well for gods/angels as for demons), then putting in a little bit of support for tying WoD Inferno and WoD Empyrean into Hunter. I wouldn't say no to some ST advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:01:52-08:00","id":413386,"title":"","content":"I want a chronicle about hunters committing to a variety of vigils. Updated mechanics would be nice too.<br /> <br /> As a fan, I'll sit and wait to see what they deliver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-20-2015, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:09:09-08:00","id":413401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=413386#post413386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a chronicle about hunter committing to a variety of vigils. Updated mechanics would be nice too.<br /> <br /> As a fan, I'll sit and wait to see what they deliver.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> Just give me more Hunter, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:52:14-08:00","id":413828,"title":"","content":"Oh, good. I wrote the OP at 4AM in the middle of a panic attack and forgot this thread existed until just now; I'm amazed it's readable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T10:00:48-08:00","id":414120,"title":"","content":"Agree with much of what's said above (though I actually kind of <i>like</i> Hunter's simplicity of approach). My own desire would be for much more support for and examples of mixed-Conspiracy/Compact hunter groups. In other words, your typical gang of PCs is going to want to play as different kinds of Hunters. How do you deal with a group of hunters that includes a TFV ex-soldier, an Ascending Ones alchemist, a MM priest, and an Ashwood Abbey playboy in a way that does not feel like barebones rationalization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T10:33:55-08:00","id":414173,"title":"","content":"NeoTiamat, we are now enemies ;p<br /> <br /> I want to go in the opposite direction. Make it clear that playing TF:V and AKD is roughly as different as playing Werewolf or Mage. And thus mixed groups should get the same level of support as a mixed group of Werewolves and Mages (I know you do that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). If it feels like barebones rationalization, that's because it really doesn't make sense for a top secret governmental military organisation to run joint operations with a sociopathic playboy. If they wanted him onboard they'd conscript him and start giving him orders, who's going to stop them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T11:16:35-08:00","id":414221,"title":"","content":"...personally I want a LOT more support for crossover play (it seems like the most obvious gap in the current literature), but that's getting a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't actually disagree with you that how it stands now, it's exceedingly weird. But the issue is that Conspiracies are to Hunter what both clan and covenant is to vampire -- Hunters already get far less in the way of 'toys' than other splats, so restricting things to a single Conspiracy/Compact reduces the possible variety further still. And in my experience, players grumble and gripe about that kind of restriction a lot (especially if they can flip through the rest of the book and see all the cool stuff they aren't allowed to have). <br /> <br /> Thinking on it... I think that if you want to make all the conspiracies dramatically separate, that could work... <i>but</i> in that case you need to give each compact and conspiracy far more in the way of development. Make it possible to have a party of four or five people from the same conspiracy, all of whom can have different and memorable suites of Endowments. You'd also want to stop making scores of new compacts and conspiracies (which I suspect also makes me your enemy now), since you'll end up with a Hunter game that is a mile wide and an inch deep -- you have what, twelve Conspiracies and twenty Compacts at the moment, but even the best developed of them have perhaps twenty pages of detailing scattered across half a dozen books, and the non-core ones have much less. It's an inefficient use of space if 95% of the material is unusable in any given game.<br /> <br /> So, I'll phrase my thoughts a bit differently. Hunter 2E could benefit from a greater conceptualization of different 'classes' in a typical Hunter party. This might come from treating the current Conspiracies and Compacts as 'classes' (in which case the setting needs to be more open to that), or it might come from expanding the diversity of roles available in a single conspiracy or compact (in which case each one needs both more setting development and a larger pool of mechanical thingies). Or one could try something else altogether, perhaps divorcing Endowments from Conspiracy/Compact, so that you could have a set of different 'classes' of Hunter all in one Conspiracy. I think making Hunter more 'Conspiracy Crossover' friendly is the <i>simplest</i> way to go about it, but it's hardly the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T12:16:54-08:00","id":414254,"title":"","content":"I don't think you need to give each class unique mechanical toys. People can and do play pure mortal games, so since mortal games provide enough toys having everyone in the MM with access the same Benediction Endowment and tactics should be sufficient. I definitely wouldn't divorce Endowments from Conspiracies, since the Endowments give each group a lot of useful flavour.<br /> <br /> As for classes, I think you're forgetting Professions. For a Compact with varied Professsions it almost writes itself. Consider a Union cell with a Cop, a Journalist, a Labourer, and an Outdoorsman. It's instantly clear how they all bring unique skills and viewpoints to the cell, while being charachters you can instantly imagine in a Midwestern small town America cell of the Union. That said, I do agree that the Conspiracies could use more expansion.<br /> <br /> In TF:V if you're fighting monsters you're basically a soldier, even if your Profession is Scientist, if you're fighting monsters TF:V treats you like a soldier and you won't really get that many opportunities to do science. Why analyse samples when you can send them of to the lab which has better equipment and more staff? But TF:V obviously has lots of scientists, where does Advanced Armoury come from, so more material that makes TF:V scientists, beurocrats, intelligence analysts, communications officers, etc playable would be a very good thing.<br /> <br /> I did something like this for the MM in the sadly stalled <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Two:_Building_a_Cult#Example:_The_Malleus_Maleficarum\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter: Cults</a> project.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I guess that I disagree that 'Conspiracy Crossover' is simple because most of the time it just makes absolutely no sense for these groups to team up. Just to start with there's several conspiracies the MM and the AKD would kill on sight for Witchcraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-21-2015, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:08:24-08:00","id":414482,"title":"","content":"I could see a 2e Hunter being a corebook that talks about Hunters <i>in general</i>, with a nice fat chapter of building antagonists, describing how to Hunters hunt things socially, etc. In other words, the first few chapters should be about Tier 1 play, with barebone frameworks for Tier 2 and Tier 3 play. It should be story-hook heavy and light on mechanics for the player side of the ST screen. Make it mostly an ST book, with territory creation stuff and whatever else they feel fit to stick in there.<br /> <br /> Then, have a free appendix (kinda like how GMC has a free appendix) that outlines the Hunter &quot;template&quot;, with a beefed-up version of the Professional Training and Mystery Cult Initiation merits, a mess of Conditions, and an updated version of The Code which works better with Integrity.<br /> <br /> Then, you get a &quot;pack&quot; of Compacts and Conspiracies; Compacts are just a few pages of fluff or whatever along with maybe a unique merit or Condition (besides their &quot;Status&quot; benefits), while Conspiracies have what Compacts get plus an Endowment section. You get the pack of &quot;core&quot; Compacts/Conspiracies as part of buying Hunter 2e...<br /> <br /> And then scatter them. You want the Cainite Heresy? Buy a copy of Vampire 2e, and you get the Cainite Heresy add-on. Promethean Brotherhood? Grab Mage 2e. They want to publish a Mysterious Places 2e? Hey, who squirrelled that Compact in there?<br /> <hr /><br /> Basically, Hunter as a full major template of its own always felt odd to me (though I love Hunter to death); why not take advantage of what Hunters are (i.e., humans that know about the Supernatural, and aren't happy about it <i>at all</i>), and spread it around liberally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:26:50-08:00","id":414578,"title":"","content":"Both Mummy Guilds and Changeling Eldrich Titles such as the Lost Pantheon are older, perhaps a lot older then mage orders and hunter conspiracies (Mummy Guilds go back to Irem and the Lost Pantheon goes back to the Stone Age).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T18:53:17-08:00","id":414739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414254#post414254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you need to give each class unique mechanical toys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly, you don't <i>need</i> to. You don't really need to do anything, Hunter 1E is a pretty successful and well-built game, with very little, I think, in the way of glaring flaws that need to be fixed (compare, say, to the issues that Werewolf has). Tighten up the mechanics, bring together the bits of lore and mechanics currently spread out around five or six books, and you're golden.<br /> <br /> That said, mechanical toys make people happy -- hence the proliferation of Conspiracies and Entitlements and Bloodlines that all give their own unique spin on stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for classes, I think you're forgetting Professions. For a Compact with varied Professsions it almost writes itself. Consider a Union cell with a Cop, a Journalist, a Labourer, and an Outdoorsman. It's instantly clear how they all bring unique skills and viewpoints to the cell, while being charachters you can instantly imagine in a Midwestern small town America cell of the Union. </div> </div> </div>I haven't forgotten them, and I think they're a very good thing. But I also think that as they stand right now, there isn't enough mechanical depth to them to really make them all unique. *taps chin, makes mental note to try some homebrew in that direction some day*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In TF:V if you're fighting monsters you're basically a soldier, even if your Profession is Scientist, if you're fighting monsters TF:V treats you like a soldier and you won't really get that many opportunities to do science. Why analyse samples when you can send them of to the lab which has better equipment and more staff? But TF:V obviously has lots of scientists, where does Advanced Armoury come from, so more material that makes TF:V scientists, beurocrats, intelligence analysts, communications officers, etc playable would be a very good thing.<br /> <br /> I did something like this for the MM in the sadly stalled <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Two:_Building_a_Cult#Example:_The_Malleus_Maleficarum\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter: Cults</a> project. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'd also like to see the Endowments possess a bit more internal variation. To take your example, having Advanced Armory endowments geared not just to shooting stuff but also to intelligence analysts or researchers or bureaucrats would be a good thing -- there's a bit of that already (just how much varies between Endowments), but one could do more here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I guess that I disagree that 'Conspiracy Crossover' is simple because most of the time it just makes absolutely no sense for these groups to team up. Just to start with there's several conspiracies the MM and the AKD would kill on sight for Witchcraft. </div> </div> </div>Well. Simple in that it would take the most advantage of the current set of material. You don't need to give TFV a huge expansion, you just need to justify TFV and MM hanging out. Calling it <i>simple</i> is not to imply that it's <i>easy</i>.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Josef Wilhelm game that predated the Changeling game you and I were so briefly a part of had my Lucifuge character trying to save some Malleus hunters, and it worked <i>amazingly</i> well. Which is what gives me hope that this is very doable. The Lucifuge and the MM would seem like the most severe of blood enemies... but their bosses have been buddies since the Middle Ages. You can do creative stuff with this.<br /> <hr /><br /> If I were to summarize my thoughts, both setting and mechanics, I think I'd say that I would like to see from Hunter 2E less breadth and more depth. I'm actually very much open to running an all-Lucifuge or an all-Cheiron game (...an all-Cheiron game sounds amazingly psychotic, actually), but I think it needs more support than the setting has at this date. Of course, if you're expanding depth, then you need to cut down on breadth (for page count if nothing else), and that means someone's ox is getting gored. Tricky, isn't it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T19:55:48-08:00","id":414791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414254#post414254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In TF:V if you're fighting monsters you're basically a soldier, even if your Profession is Scientist, if you're fighting monsters TF:V treats you like a soldier and you won't really get that many opportunities to do science. Why analyse samples when you can send them of to the lab which has better equipment and more staff? But TF:V obviously has lots of scientists, where does Advanced Armoury come from, so more material that makes TF:V scientists, beurocrats, intelligence analysts, communications officers, etc playable would be a very good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you're forgetting that there are two &quot;tribes&quot; in TF:V. The <i>Suits </i>and the <i>SWAT. </i>The SWAT guys are your paramilitary type that go in guns blazing and are all soldiers. Suits are more like FBI agents of the Supernatural; the MIB. They drive around in a black muscle car with a boot full of high-tech devices. One might indeed be a scientist and might have a portable lab of high-tech analysis equipment for quick sample analysis and ENE identification. Quite frankly, I always thought that the Suits felt more Hunter than the SWAT guys anyway. They always felt like foils and antagonists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T21:24:03-08:00","id":414853,"title":"","content":"I'd want more dread powers, if I want hunters to be up against giant ants or tentacled mutant brains to the invisible man or a giant bug monster, I want the powers to cover it.<br /> <br /> Expanded endowment systems would be useful too, for building do it yourself conspiracies, to minor advantages like those given the compacts in C&amp;C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T22:00:27-08:00","id":414909,"title":"","content":"Information supporting the middle part of a hunter chronicle. What sort of effect are hunters having on the world around them? How are they coping with their growing experience and knowledge weighed against their degrading morality?<br /> <br /> A hunter endgame, or various endgame scenarios, with a page or two discussing how to properly finish a hunter chronicle. It doesn't have to be on a victory on a global scale (though information on that possibility would be welcome). But a possibility of campaign ending victory (bittersweet as it may be) or resolution (as intensely personal as it might be) would be most welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T23:26:11-08:00","id":414951,"title":"","content":"Total Overhaul of the Tactics system. I think it's needlessly complicated, overly burdened with prerequisites and a lot of &quot;Wait, what? Why?&quot; decisions. Tactical fatigue needs to go. Requiring multiple people needs to go. Bonuses for arbitrarily selected compacts and conspiracies need to go. A tactic, ideally, is either a permission to let an extended action do something it normally could not (a working exorcism, for example), guarantees a particular outcome or side effect occurs/does not occur (for example, &quot;Controlled Immolation: Fires started by the hunters are assumed to be controlled...&quot;) or otherwise modifies the stakes of teamwork/extended action rolls, rather than affecting them directly. &quot;Disappear&quot; is a signal from players to ST they don't want to be captured. I would see them more like group controlled Conditions than anything else, with an optional &quot;Take a beat to have a Tactical Failure - Disappear means someone is followed or captured, etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> Someone needs to think about the Aegis Kai Doru. I think some kind of Endowment relating to <i>forging</i> artifacts of legend makes more sense. I mean, in theory &quot;Relic&quot; is <i>already</i> a merit available to regular World of Darkness characters and any of the conspiracies might come across something.<br /> <br /> The Compact/Conspiracy divide needs to die. A build-your-own conspiracy system could scale up from regional groups without an endowment or institutional longevity, to the really powerful conspiracies that might have <i>more than one</i> Endowment. Make the system more flexible and interesting. We'll be building our own Courts in Changeling 2e; lets build our own conspiracies in Hunter 2e.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T04:38:40-08:00","id":415023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414739#post414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't forgotten them, and I think they're a very good thing. But I also think that as they stand right now, there isn't enough mechanical depth to them to really make them all unique. *taps chin, makes mental note to try some homebrew in that direction some day*</div> </div> </div> </div> What mechanical depth do you think they need? To me the benefits of playing a Cop, while undefined, are obvious. Weaponry training, access to info, authority. Etc.<br /> <br /> Most of them probably don't require specal mechanics either. A cop badge is just an equipment bonus in some circumstances and different NPC reations in others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414739#post414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lucifuge and the MM would seem like the most severe of blood enemies... but their bosses have been buddies since the Middle Ages. You can do creative stuff with this.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can do creative stuff like this once or twice, but do it too many times and it breaks plausibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414739#post414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I think it needs more support than the setting has at this date. Of course, if you're expanding depth, then you need to cut down on breadth (for page count if nothing else), and that means someone's ox is getting gored. Tricky, isn't it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Compacts and Conspiracies PDF should have been IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T08:11:01-08:00","id":415143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415023#post415023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What mechanical depth do you think they need? To me the benefits of playing a Cop, while undefined, are obvious. Weaponry training, access to info, authority. Etc.<br /> <br /> Most of them probably don't require specal mechanics either. A cop badge is just an equipment bonus in some circumstances and different NPC reations in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is wandering out of the territory which I have well thought out, but I think greater differentiation would be nice. Perhaps a capstone or unique ability per Profession (access to weaponry for soldiers and arrest powers for cops are what come to mind off the top of my head). Again, this isn't <i>necessary</i>, don't get me wrong. But I think it would be a nice addition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can do creative stuff like this once or twice, but do it too many times and it breaks plausibility. </div> </div> </div>This comes down to personal taste. For me, whatever plausibility there is has already died in a gutter once you assume there are just under forty global or national anti-monster groups out there, and no one's blown the Masquerade wide open. So I'm willing to kick it while it's down a few times for the sake of playability.<br /> <br /> For that matter, one might look at it the other way. Many of these are large, widespread, powerful organizations that have been around for at the very <i>least</i> decades if not centuries or even millennia and are involved in broadly the same business and are all more or less on the same (anti-vampire/werewolf/witch) side. They must have encountered one another, they must have established some kind of diplomatic relations with one another, there must be some sort of <i>policy</i> in these organizations for what you do when you encounter members of other organizations -- something more developed than the kinda vague 'Stereotypes' bits that we get. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what the Compacts and Conspiracies PDF should have been IMO. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. To be fair, it did do a pretty decent job of it, within the limits of its page count.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:50:46-08:00","id":415340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415143#post415143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a capstone or unique ability per Profession (access to weaponry for soldiers and arrest powers for cops are what come to mind off the top of my head).</div> </div> </div> </div> You see, to me they already have all this stuff. It's not an explicit mechanical perk, but do you really need to be told that a cop has the power to arrest people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415143#post415143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes down to personal taste. For me, whatever plausibility there is has already died in a gutter once you assume there are just under forty global or national anti-monster groups out there, and no one's blown the Masquerade wide open. So I'm willing to kick it while it's down a few times for the sake of playability.</div> </div> </div> </div> The way I see it, every setting is aloud to have &quot;one big lie&quot;.<br /> <br /> For Hunter that big lie is that monster hunters, and their prey, exist in secret and have done for centuries. But if you then portray those monsters or monster hunters activing in unrealistic ways that would break my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> A secret Men in Black division in the USA government that hunts monsters. Sure. A secret Men in Black division who work as equal partners with a group of average joe monster hunters, that breaks my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415143#post415143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, one might look at it the other way. Many of these are large, widespread, powerful organizations that have been around for at the very <i>least</i> decades if not centuries or even millennia and are involved in broadly the same business and are all more or less on the same (anti-vampire/werewolf/witch) side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they'll encounter each other, establish diplomatic relationships. That I have no problem with. It's the specifics of the relationship that matter. I think you'll have more open wars and cold wars than cases where it would be seen as acceptable to have a mixed cell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:25:12-08:00","id":415899,"title":"","content":"I want a redefinition of the tiers: in 1e, it\u2019s an uncomfortable conflation of \u201chow well organized are the hunters?\u201d and \u201cwhat style of game are you playing?\u201d The assumption is that if you\u2019re playing an isolated cell, you\u2019re also playing \u201chunters as regular mortals in over their heads\u201d; if you\u2019re playing with compacts, you\u2019re also playing \u201chunters as competent mortals who hold their own\u201d; and if you\u2019re playing with conspiracies, you\u2019re also playing \u201chunters who dabble in the supernatural and blur the line between human and monster\u201d. <br /> <br /> In 2e, I\u2019d like these tight couplings of concepts to be considerably loosened, ranging from talking about the different play styles and the mechanics that support them independently of the different organizational tiers to recasting some existing Conspiracies as Compacts and vice versa (<i>without</i> any change as to whether or not they offer supernatural Endowments) to providing advice on how to use various orgs in chronicles that are set up with a different playstyle than the one for which the org was originally conceived. <br /> <br /> On the first point, there are a number of ideas from previous books (mainly <b>Mirrors</b> and <b>Strange Dead Love</b>) that I\u2019d like to see introduced into <b>Hunter</b> as optional rules, in much the same way that 1e presented the Code as an optional rule: for \u201ccompetent mortals\u201d, I wouldn\u2019t mind an optional system of \u201cedges\u201d that can be acquired through Practical Experience ranging from skill tricks to trait boosts and maybe even additional uses for willpower; for \u201cborderline supernaturals\u201d, I\u2019d like to see GMC-style refinements of Conviction and Forbidden Knowledge (<i>also</i> tied explicitly to Practical Experience; and in the latter case, presented in the context of Dread Powers). The key would be to clearly section them off as playstyle-specific rules that are optional even when the requisite playstyle is in effect, and to stress repeatedly that if you don\u2019t like any of these rules options, you don\u2019t have to use them. <br /> <br /> In effect, <b>Hunter</b> is three \u201cgames\u201d in one: it can be used as if it were a \u201cblue book supplement\u201d that introduces new organizations and tools for mortal protagonists to take advantage of; it can be used to portray a \u201cspecial breed\u201d of mortals who have been set apart from your average denizen of the World of Darkness by the fact that they\u2019ve encountered the supernatural and not turned away; or it can be used to handle mortals who fight the monsters using every tool they can get their hands on, even at the risk of becoming monsters themselves. I\u2019d like to see this three-way conceptual division made more explicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:35:35-08:00","id":415910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415340#post415340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, every setting is aloud to have &quot;one big lie&quot;... A secret Men in Black division in the USA government that hunts monsters. Sure. A secret Men in Black division who work as equal partners with a group of average joe monster hunters, that breaks my suspension of disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, personal taste then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, they'll encounter each other, establish diplomatic relationships. That I have no problem with. It's the specifics of the relationship that matter. I think you'll have more open wars and cold wars than cases where it would be seen as acceptable to have a mixed cell. </div> </div> </div>I suspect the <i>best</i> way to handle this sort of thing would be to make it modular. You want your Lucifuge and MM to be blood enemies, you can do that. Want them allies, you can do that. So the relations <i>will</i> be a mixture of alliance, friendly neutrality, cold war, and open war... but the specific dynamics will be determined by the preferences of your game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In effect, <b>Hunter</b> is three \u201cgames\u201d in one: it can be used as if it were a \u201cblue book supplement\u201d that introduces new organizations and tools for mortal protagonists to take advantage of; it can be used to portray a \u201cspecial breed\u201d of mortals who have been set apart from your average denizen of the World of Darkness by the fact that they\u2019ve encountered the supernatural and not turned away; or it can be used to handle mortals who fight the monsters using every tool they can get their hands on, even at the risk of becoming monsters themselves. I\u2019d like to see this three-way conceptual division made more explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this rather nicely puts something into words that I'd been thinking. Hunter can be.... Ticked-Off-Joe-Normal: The Crowbarring, or it can be Illuminati: The Secret Societying. I mean, look away from the monster hunting angle, and you've got the American government, satanists, the Catholics, a Megacorp, Islamic terrorist types, and a Greco-Roman cult, all with global reach and resources and what have you. It makes for some interesting possibilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:01:52-08:00","id":415938,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d go so far as to say that if you\u2019re playing in Ticked Off Joe Normal: the Crowbarring mode, you probably shouldn\u2019t even have Risking Willpower at your disposal, and <i>maybe</i> not even Practical Experience; these are both mechanics designed to emphasize hunters as a cut above your average mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:41:57-08:00","id":415989,"title":"","content":"What do Tiers mean? I know in my mind, of course, but the fact that The Union probably outnumbers the Lucifuge exponentially, Tier starts to lose meaning.<br /> <br /> I mostly just want to see high Tier mean something. Using the two groups above, The Union shouldn't just have hunter-net; they should have safehouses in caches across the country, easy means of travel, and lots of contacts. The Lucifuge isn't just demon powers, it's an ancient library of demonological knowledge, the ability to hide being hellspawn from everyone who wants them dead for it, and tons of easy air travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:47:50-08:00","id":415997,"title":"","content":"Exactly: what <i>do</i> Tiers mean? Bear in mind that GMC took the concept and applied a radically different meaning to it than Hunter did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:50:52-08:00","id":416003,"title":"","content":"A less regional focus would be nice for a 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> I mean.. in games that aren't set in the United States, three factions in the game are just plain not working.<br /> The Long Night, the Union and Task Force: Valkyrie are all pretty well American through-and-through. And while it isn't too much of a problem to make up regional versions of them (at least not the latter two), it'd be nice if the games wasn't basically saying that you should play them in the United States, or else make up your own fluff. I mean.. which factions work in a game set in say.. Hong Kong? Off my head it's *most* of the Conspiracies. TF:V, however, is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:57:28-08:00","id":416034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=415997#post415997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly: what <i>do</i> Tiers mean? Bear in mind that GMC took the concept and applied a radically different meaning to it than Hunter did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tier in Hunter is a bizarre idea of magical power and organizational strength. Tier in everything else is a sense of scale. You can totally do a &quot;Tier 3&quot; Union game just as easily as you can do a Tier 1 VALKYRIE game.<br /> <br /> Another hope; more internationality. We have almost exclusively American groups (and no Native ones, seriously?), and the closest we get to a non-Western group is the Ascending Ones. Does nobody fight monsters in Asia? Does the only Muslim group need to be hiding in a Vampire supplement? Does every religious group need to be Abrahamic?<br /> <br /> EDIT: And we need more monsters! Everyone knows what vampires are; give me skinless creatures that eat dreams or spooky alien brain parasites. Alternatively; do what the upcoming Demon Storyteller's Guide is gonna do, and reinvent all the splats through the eyes of Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-22-2015, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:24:23-08:00","id":416050,"title":"","content":"Could we please ditch the numeric labels for the Tiers in 2e? Instead of talking \u201cTier 1, Tier 2, Tier 3\u201d, go with GMC\u2019s \u201cLocal, Regional, Global\u201d terminology \u2014 and revise the Conspiracies so that they <i>are</i> Global, or demote them to Regional status. <br /> <br /> Just as importantly, decouple them from individual power level. Here, Tier 1, 2, and 3 might translate to, say, Gritty, Cinematic, and Empowered. There would still be a loose coupling here: <br /> <br /> \u2022 isolated cells would tend to be featured in Local chronicles and would tend to feature Gritty protagonists<br /> \u2022 Compacts would tend to be featured in Regional chronicles and would tend to feature Cinematic protagonists<br /> \u2022 Conspiracies would tend to be featured in Global chronicles and would tend to feature Empowered protagonists<br /> <br /> But those would only be tendencies: you could easily have a Regional chronicle featuring an independent cell of Empowered hunters, or a Global chronicle featuring Gritty hunters who belong to Compacts.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, 1e effectively only has two \u201cpersonal power\u201d Tiers: if you\u2019re not Empowered, you\u2019re mostly Gritty with a touch of Cinematic. This, too, is a conflation that I want to see ditched: let those who like playinng Hunter at the Gritty tier go <i>purely</i> Gritty, without any \u201ccheats\u201d to make life easier on them (not even Risking Willpower); and let those who like playing Hunter at the Cinematic tier go beyond what <b>Hunter 1e</b> allowed hunters without supernatural resources to do, into the realm of <b>Strange Dead Love</b>\u2019s Heroic Mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-22-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:27:36-08:00","id":416052,"title":"","content":"That's really a neat way to put it. Well done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:36:57-08:00","id":416078,"title":"","content":"And yes; if WoD2e doesn\u2019t give us tools for what <b>Glimpses of the Unknown</b> called \u201cOutsiders\u201d (and, given that it\u2019s apparently featuring the God-Machine Chronicle, it may not), <b>Mage 2e</b> definitely should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-22-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:57:17-08:00","id":416084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=416078#post416078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe instead of Amateur, Professional, and Empowered, the terms should be Gritty, Cinematic, and Empowered. The point is, numeric terms aren\u2019t descriptive and facilitate ambiguity; <i>named</i> Tiers can be much more clear about what they\u2019re trying to describe.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Trail of Cthulhu</i> divides the game between Purist play (the supernatural will either kill you or drive you insane) and Pulp play (you can kill the supernatural with Tommy guns and dynamite). Hunter would benefit from a similar decision; are the player characters struggling against an overwhelming threat, or are they kicking in the door of the vampire's haven and burning it to death with homemade flamethrowers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:27:34-08:00","id":416136,"title":"","content":"The point is that it\u2019s a decision that the Storyteller should make, and the game designers should facilitate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:28:01-08:00","id":416214,"title":"","content":"Maybe something to deal with the whole Biblical Hunters I've been hearing about? I don't know if anyone else is on board with it, but the idea of looking at the world of a hunter back when hunter was one of the most valuable jobs in the world feels like something worth looking into, especially with all the ancient heroes that could double as hunters or slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:19:37-08:00","id":417599,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that three-way split works. I could see a ragtag bunch of normal people still having storylines involving supernatural empowerment; given the various side-effects and consequences of supernatural powers, or how low-key they might be, I don't necessarily think &quot;has powers/endowments/supernatural merits&quot; is on the same axis as the level of institutional or organizational support they might have. The normal person with psychic visions compelling them to investigate the supernatural is a Tier 1 concept despite some degree of empowerment.<br /> <br /> There are really two tiers - one where the resources available to the group are literally the combined resources available to each individual hunter (as in, &quot;just the cell&quot;) and one where there's organizational support and resources available to the group. Compact to Conspiracy is just a matter of degree.<br /> <br /> So I'd abandon Compacts/Tier 2 as a distinct tier, and just go with Tier 1 and Tier 3 (though you wouldn't still use those terms). The availability of Endowments and the like would be a &quot;bolt-on&quot; to either tier. Make room for Tier 1 hunters who have come across a Relic or a Tier 3 Conspiracy that lacks an Endowment.<br /> <br /> I do like the Regional/Global split for Conspiracies, but I think that could be reflected by a build-your-own-conspiracy system that measures &quot;reach.&quot; And I wouldn't say either level mitigates or has less of a chance to act as a horror setting. Hunter works as an ongoing game, which does lend itself to allowing a certain degree of survival and success by the players, since otherwise they're dead at the end of the story, and it works this way at any tier. On that note, perhaps deeper systems or guidance for all the many things you can lose other than your life. The Vigil demands sacrifice, after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:02:58-08:00","id":417626,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea of a pure/pulp split. To me one of the cool things is that both exist side by side in the same setting. A group of factory workers struggle alone to keep a vampire from taking over their factory and squeezing the workers dry; but that same vampire fears the government blowing up his haven with attack helicopters.<br /> <br /> I'd split Endowments away from the Tiers system and thus rearange the tiers a bit (Lucifuge would be Tier 2 for example) but keep the concept as it is. Tier 1 you're alone against the darkness. Tier 2 you have allies, resources and lore. A fighting chance against a real threat but no more than that. Tier 3, monsters fear you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:39:00-08:00","id":418302,"title":"","content":"Professor Phobos: I don\u2019t know if your post was intended as a response to mine or just a critique of [b]Hunter 1e[/i]; I\u2019ve proceeded on the former assumption. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=417599#post417599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that three-way split works. I could see a ragtag bunch of normal people still having storylines involving supernatural empowerment; given the various side-effects and consequences of supernatural powers, or how low-key they might be, I don't necessarily think \u201chas powers/endowments/supernatural merits\u201d is on the same axis as the level of institutional or organizational support they might have. The normal person with psychic visions compelling them to investigate the supernatural is a Tier 1 concept despite some degree of empowerment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a Local chronicle (per the terminology given in <b>GMC</b>) featuring Empowered protagonists. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=417599#post417599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are really two tiers - one where the resources available to the group are literally the combined resources available to each individual hunter (as in, \u201cjust the cell\u201d) and one where there's organizational support and resources available to the group. Compact to Conspiracy is just a matter of degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Cell to Compact is <i>also</i> just a matter of degree. In the case of an isolated cell, you\u2019ve dialed the \u201creach\u201d down as far as it can go; but you\u2019re still dealing with the same <i>concept</i> of \u201chow much \u2018reach\u2019 do the protagonists have?\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=417599#post417599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'd abandon Compacts/Tier 2 as a distinct tier, and just go with Tier 1 and Tier 3 (though you wouldn't still use those terms). The availability of Endowments and the like would be a \u201cbolt-on\u201d to either tier. Make room for Tier 1 hunters who have come across a Relic or a Tier 3 Conspiracy that lacks an Endowment.<br /> <br /> I do like the Regional/Global split for Conspiracies, but I think that could be reflected by a build-your-own-conspiracy system that measures \u201creach.\u201d And I wouldn't say either level mitigates or has less of a chance to act as a horror setting. Hunter works as an ongoing game, which does lend itself to allowing a certain degree of survival and success by the players, since otherwise they're dead at the end of the story, and it works this way at any tier. On that note, perhaps deeper systems or guidance for all the many things you can lose other than your life. The Vigil demands sacrifice, after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>I notice that you keep talking about \u201ctier\u201d in terms of \u201chow extensive are the resources the troupe has to draw upon?\u201d That does seem to be the notion that 1e was using when it conceived of the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy split; but that\u2019s not really the notion that GMC is going for with its Local/Regional/Global/Cosmic split: there, the focus is less on the protagonists\u2019 resources and more on the scope of the chronicle\u2019s consequences: to give an extreme example, you can <i>easily</i> have a lone(ly) troupe in a chronicle where the fate of the world hangs in the balance \u2014 that is, a Cell of hunters at the heart of a Cosmic chronicle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=417626#post417626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea of a pure/pulp split. To me one of the cool things is that both exist side by side in the same setting. A group of factory workers struggle alone to keep a vampire from taking over their factory and squeezing the workers dry; but that same vampire fears the government blowing up his haven with attack helicopters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s got nothing to do with \u201cpure/pulp\u201d; that\u2019s a matter of \u201ccell/compact\u201d \u2014 as with Professor Phobos, you\u2019re talking in terms of the troupe\u2019s \u201creach\u201d; and mixing different groups with different \u201creaches\u201d in a single chronicle is entirely reasonable. I\u2019m thinking of \u201cgritty/cinematic\u201d being on a separate axis from that; it has to do with whether the protagonists themselves are to be portrayed as ordinary people or as extraordinary people. I put \u201cempowered\u201d at the top of that axis, not because ordinary and exraordinary people can never have supernatural abilities (they can), but because \u201cyou <i>are</i> borderline supernatural\u201d is the logical conclusion of that progression. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=417626#post417626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd split Endowments away from the Tiers system and thus rearange the tiers a bit (Lucifuge would be Tier 2 for example) but keep the concept as it is. Tier 1 you're alone against the darkness. Tier 2 you have allies, resources and lore. A fighting chance against a real threat but no more than that. Tier 3, monsters fear you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The folks at Onyx Path don\u2019t see things that way, which is why they redefined Tiers in GMC. But the original concept that you outline here still works as the basis for the distinction between Cells, Compacts, and Conspiracies; and to that extent, I agree that it should be kept. But just as \u201cdo you have supernatural powers?\u201d ought to be decoupled at least partially from \u201chow much of a support network and resources do you have?\u201d, the latter ought to be at least partially decoupled from \u201cwhat is the chronicle\u2019s scope?\u201d \u2014 which is the essence of GMC-style Tiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-24-2015, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T00:41:31-08:00","id":418488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=418302#post418302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s got nothing to do with \u201cpure/pulp\u201d; that\u2019s a matter of \u201ccell/compact\u201d \u2014 as with Professor Phobos, you\u2019re talking in terms of the troupe\u2019s \u201creach\u201d; and mixing different groups with different \u201creaches\u201d in a single chronicle is entirely reasonable. I\u2019m thinking of \u201cgritty/cinematic\u201d being on a separate axis from that; it has to do with whether the protagonists themselves are to be portrayed as ordinary people or as extraordinary people. I put \u201cempowered\u201d at the top of that axis, not because ordinary and exraordinary people can never have supernatural abilities (they can), but because \u201cyou <i>are</i> borderline supernatural\u201d is the logical conclusion of that progression.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I don't think of empowerement being a gritty/cinematic axis. Just a powerless/powerful axis. VASCU are empowered, but you can (and probably should) play them as a gritty police procedual, where you know the monster cannot survive a SWAT team. But can the detectives find the Slasher before his next victim dies? The MM might be able to take down a Vampire Prince and his entire court, but put them up against an Archdemon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:45:52-08:00","id":418568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=418488#post418488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't think of empowerement being a gritty/cinematic axis. Just a powerless/powerful axis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then \u201cempowerment\u201d isn\u2019t the right term for what I\u2019m talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:53:38-08:00","id":418572,"title":"","content":"I very much like the local/regional/global/cosmic spread. I don't necessarily think we need an &quot;Empowered/Not Empowered&quot; bolt-on sort of modifier, because individual hunters in a group may or may not avail themselves of the various supernatural merits; they're already purchased from the same pool of XP and moderated by ST/group consensus anyway. A local group of Hunters, one of whom is a telekinetic, is neither in the &quot;Empowered&quot; category (because, say, the other four hunters don't have any) and not really in the &quot;Depowered&quot; category either.<br /> <br /> Some conspiracies just teach certain kinds of supernatural merits. I would favor allowing the conspiracy system the flexibility to have, say, a local group that has an Endowment (the genius loci of the creepy small town Whisper Lake guides its defenders to defend the residents; the Archangel Lesser Magellanic Cloud condensed into mortal form over this stretch of African Savannah and if you have lived off the soil, animals and water of the area for a year and a day some part of you is becomes part of the Archangel...) and a global (i.e., &quot;Tier 3 Conspiracy&quot;) group that doesn't have one (NATO's Office of Special Contingencies is an international security service whose mission is to keep NATO forces and command structure free of supernatural influence; the Chasseurs sans Frontieres track down monsters and coordinate hunts across borders).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:19:14-08:00","id":418692,"title":"","content":"Just to throw it in, but Trails of Cthulhu's <i>Bookhounds of London</i> had something a bit like this -- in addition to Pulp/Purist approaches, they also had three tones available for the game (Arabesque, which was sort of faerie tale, Technicolor, which was Hammer Horror-ish, and Sordid, which was basically about how scummy things could get) and discussed a bit how to tweak the game to support any variety. What was interesting was that they did this without any real mechanical rules or what-not. They just had a few pages discussing how the setting would look with each tone, about half a page of plothooks, and the dozen or so NPCs were presented with brief variations on the theme. So the sleepless book hunter was a heroin addict in Sordid and was cursed in Technicolor. <br /> <br /> So discussions and allowances of different tones doesn't <i>have</i> to be terribly complex or require enormous page counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:27:30-08:00","id":420580,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second what <b>Dataweaver </b>has been saying, basically, since it more or less covers the direction I'd like Hunter to go, and addresses the issues I see in it now. The scope of an organization and the capabilities the individual hunters posses should be two different axes.<br /> <br /> However, a rethinking of the Tactics system like <b>Professor Phobos </b>suggested is also a consideration. I feel like the existing one doesn't really do the concept justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:01:01-08:00","id":420764,"title":"","content":"Definitely break open and break down the creation of a new organization. Show us how a conspiracy is born. Show us how a compact dies. Give us tools and suggestions for making them, and then provide some great examples. Including some from outside the US of A.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed having 'mundane' endowments like popped up in C&amp;C and would love to see them more central. As much as they represent resources they seem to me to represent <i>methodology</i>. I could see some organizations having both methodologies and specific power endowments.<br /> <br /> (Pet peeve: of all the main organizations I think the AKD need to most love and care in a revamp. Their oath really limits the stories you can tell with them and is an odd fit with the real meat of the organization, which is that they're relic-hunters.)<br /> <br /> Also agree re: the tactics system. It's got too much fiddle and not enough punch. The differing prices for different tiers is unnecessary. It should be easier to come up with some. These should feel like an advantage to have and they should shape how a mortal hunter's hunt works differently from a hunting vampire or a hunting werewolf.<br /> <br /> More variety in how they interact with the supernatural, not just in how they approach it (kill v. study etc) but in the relationships they forge with it. I want to see compacts who are knowing and willing allies of Supernatural X in the interest of fighting Supernatural Y. I want to see compacts who are temporary allies of Supernatural Z and planning to stab them in the back. I definitely want to see deeper and more nuanced takes on hunters who want to <i>become</i> supernatural.<br /> <br /> I think all of that would come together really well with a smattering of different example cities with very different vigils going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:33:15-08:00","id":420953,"title":"","content":"If there's something I want to see, it's honestly more to do with the paranoia of the different groups. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of keeping 1st tier &quot;bunch of guys got their shotguns and started shooting at the things they heard go bump in the night&quot; being about ignorance and paranoia of the supernatural, but making the 3rd tier heavy hitters have a different theme. <br /> <br /> Think of it like the difference between <i>Alien </i>and <i>Aliens</i>. In <i>Alien</i>, there's only one monster, but the nearly-helpless cast can't do much to stop even that, and it makes the single xenomorph build a creeping, paranoid tension. In <i>Aliens</i>, you have marines with miniguns mowing down dozens of the beasts like it's nothing, and it has this huge adrenal rush sense of an action hero movie more than a horror film. In fact, I watched <i>Aliens</i> with my parents repeatedly, along with <i>Top Gun</i> (fast-forwarding the boring talking scenes to get back to the cool jet planes), when I was just 4 or so years old because it was about tough marines blasting the acid out of a whole bunch of bad guys, WHOOO! The idea of it being scary just didn't even enter my mind. <br /> <br /> If you're playing <i>Ride of the Valkyries</i> while your Task Force: VALKYRIE platoon drops in on a werewolf compound with Blackhawks and Apache helicopters firing silver-shrapnel launching TOW missiles and dual-wielding M-16s while shirtless (gotta show off that six-pack!) and wearing an American Flag bandana... you're not fooling anyone calling it a &quot;horror game&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> Rather, I'm actually against the notion of having completely segregated &quot;compromised&quot; and &quot;uncompromised&quot; conspiracies, the way Kings Raven suggested. I think it makes for the game balance to have each different conspiracy have its own little paranoia in its own little weird way. Rather than the whole of VALKYRIE being a vampire front, make a branch of it compromised, and have the players have to navigate the bureaucracy to isolate the infected cells... and find a way to get into a position where they can actually accuse or eliminate a superior officer without being branded traitor, or tipping the target off so you get liquidated, yourselves, first. <br /> <br /> In fact, I think it's kind of the point of Hunter that the conspiracies are at least as morally murky as the monsters they are supposedly hunting. As written, the only group that's an unambiguous team of good-guys is VASCU. (And they're mostly there as the heroic antagonists of a game where you purposefully play unabashed pure evil characters, not primarily written to be played.) Having the option of playing &quot;everything we do is perfectly morally justifiable!&quot; Ashwood Abbey kind of misses the whole point of Ashkwood Abbey. There's a Hunter conspiracy based purely around being a group of cannibals trying to steal enlightenment from eating other people's brains!<br /> <br /> The conflicting goals of the conspiracies make them interesting. Surely, a fight against the &quot;monsters&quot; of Cheiron can be as interesting as a fight against a vampire. Just because they're all humans doesn't mean they share goals, and when goals conflict between armed, paranoid people to whom violence is a way of life, then violence will prevail. If you're playing the Stonemasons, you have to watch out for Illuminati spies as well as the Witches.<br /> <br /> The smaller tiers have little equipment or training or knowledge, but they are at least &quot;pure&quot; in their cause, while choosing the conspiracies means getting power and knowledge of your supposed enemy at the cost of losing knowledge of the trustworthiness of your allies, and total control of your destiny. You can have your <i>Ride of the Valkyries</i> moment, but in between comes the uncertainty of whether your superior officer is sucking down leech juice, and maybe you should frag this guy... <i>or is that just what the witches WANT you to think?!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:27:32-08:00","id":421440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=420953#post420953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, I'm actually against the notion of having completely segregated &quot;compromised&quot; and &quot;uncompromised&quot; conspiracies, the way Kings Raven suggested. I think it makes for the game balance to have each different conspiracy have its own little paranoia in its own little weird way. Rather than the whole of VALKYRIE being a vampire front, make a branch of it compromised, and have the players have to navigate the bureaucracy to isolate the infected cells... and find a way to get into a position where they can actually accuse or eliminate a superior officer without being branded traitor, or tipping the target off so you get liquidated, yourselves, first.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that if the book is called &quot;hunter&quot;, playing an internal affairs crisis is off topic. The book promised monster hunting, not beaurocratic politics.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's fun if you want to do something different (so's your Stonemasons vs Illuminati idea later), but it shouldn't be the assumed method of play.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want to preserve Tier 3 horror, you can do it with bigger monsters. The Laundry series of books by Charles Stross are an excelent example of this, showing how Tier 3 horror is different yet workable from Tier 1 horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=420953#post420953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I think it's kind of the point of Hunter that the conspiracies are at least as morally murky as the monsters they are supposedly hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, but they don't need to be compromised by monsters to do that. Humans have no end of morally murky deeds to their name. The Ascending Ones control drug cartels. You don't need a Mummy to make that morally wrong.<br /> <br /> I think it would be much better if you worried about the fact that your commander asked you to eliminate a Network Zero guy for knowing too much - he's not a monster, it's cold blooded murder - than worrying that your commander is sucking the leach juice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:36:17-08:00","id":421445,"title":"","content":"Internal corruption of the Laundry has been a plot point like three times, though. &quot;Enemy within&quot; stories are natural for the Conspiracy level hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:47:27-08:00","id":421454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=421440#post421440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that if the book is called &quot;hunter&quot;, playing an internal affairs crisis is off topic. The book promised monster hunting, not beaurocratic politics.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's fun if you want to do something different (so's your Stonemasons vs Illuminati idea later), but it shouldn't be the assumed method of play.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want to preserve Tier 3 horror, you can do it with bigger monsters. The Laundry series of books by Charles Stross are an excelent example of this, showing how Tier 3 horror is different yet workable from Tier 1 horror.<br /> <br /> Sure, but they don't need to be compromised by monsters to do that. Humans have no end of morally murky deeds to their name. The Ascending Ones control drug cartels. You don't need a Mummy to make that morally wrong.<br /> <br /> I think it would be much better if you worried about the fact that your commander asked you to eliminate a Network Zero guy for knowing too much - he's not a monster, it's cold blooded murder - than worrying that your commander is sucking the leach juice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an Internal Affairs plotline is off-topic, why is it hinted at in basically every conspiracy in the current edition? For that matter, bureaucratic politics is also part and parcel of a conspiracy, and the way that it is portrayed in Hunter. I'm just saying they carry it to its conclusion, and make more support for plotlines involving both basic monster hunting and scouring your agency for moles. The problem is that too many plots that are exactly the same get tired, so having a larger diversity in plot types is a positive, not a negative. You can always just choose to focus only on non-stop Rambo-style raids if you really want (and your ST agrees), but support for something other than repetitive orc-slaying for their pies is something a lot of people might prefer to have as an alternative.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I'm a little confused by what you're arguing in the first and second halves of this post; First, you say that we shouldn't be playing bureaucratic infighting or internal affairs, but then you say that we should be doing internal affairs, but remove the whole &quot;monster influence over your superior officer&quot; thing that actually relates it to monsters in the first place... That sounds exactly like what you just argued against, and a lot like the sort of things I was arguing for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T01:35:26-08:00","id":421474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=421454#post421454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And honestly, I'm a little confused by what you're arguing in the first and second halves of this post; First, you say that we shouldn't be playing bureaucratic infighting or internal affairs, but then you say that we should be doing internal affairs, but remove the whole &quot;monster influence over your superior officer&quot; thing that actually relates it to monsters in the first place... That sounds exactly like what you just argued against, and a lot like the sort of things I was arguing for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets start here.<br /> <br /> The difference is that in yours you assumed that players would be fighting their own Conspiracy, or at least rogue members of their Conspiracy. In mine I'm saying that Conspiracies will do bad stuff, but players will at best be keeping their heads down and going along with it (e.g. A Knife of Paradise hunter who takes drug money and dosn't ask questions about it) or at worst complicit in the crimes (playing a Jagged Crescent smuggler could be fun).<br /> <br /> Underlying that difference is that I want humans, not monsters, to be responsible for the Conspiracies crimes. TF:V murders Network Zero Hunters in cold blood because they threaten America's ecconomic interests with those inconvinient truths; not because vampires are worried about being outed on youtube.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=421454#post421454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can always just choose to focus only on non-stop Rambo-style raids if you really want (and your ST agrees), but support for something other than repetitive orc-slaying for their pies is something a lot of people might prefer to have as an alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div> And where did I or anyone say there's only one style of play for kiling monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:04:05-08:00","id":422276,"title":"","content":"Another thing I'd like to see are some new compacts and conspiracies; I thought it was a real shame Mortal Remains didn't have a pair for Promethean, Changeling, and Geist. I feel like you could cut down the space taken by them to one page, including their stats under our hypothetical &quot;conspiracy-builder&quot; system. I'm thinking something only somewhat more elaborate than Mummy's cult system. Maybe three - Mundane Reach, Supernatural Clout, and organizational integrity. <br /> <br /> Oh, and you know what else? Someone needs to get on variety in naming. Talbot Group AND Cheiron Group? Why not call it the Talbot Foundation or the Talbot Institute? Promethean AND Illuminated Brotherhoods? Knights of St. George AND the Knights of St. Adrian? C'mon guys, variety is the spice of life.<br /> <br /> While I'm on the soapbox, the Les Mysteres can <i>happily</i> just be an Afro-Caribbean conspiracy that has an endowment for dealing with spirits. They really tried to split he difference by making it this generic spirit-hunter/cult thing when you wouldn't have tried to do that with any of the western groups - the Malleus Maleficarum is specifically Catholic for a reason. Specificity is <i>good</i>, because no one actually goes around forming generic organizations with generic goals across cultural lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-27-2015, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:41:53-08:00","id":422388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=421474#post421474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lets start here.<br /> <br /> The difference is that in yours you assumed that players would be fighting their own Conspiracy, or at least rogue members of their Conspiracy. In mine I'm saying that Conspiracies will do bad stuff, but players will at best be keeping their heads down and going along with it (e.g. A Knife of Paradise hunter who takes drug money and dosn't ask questions about it) or at worst complicit in the crimes (playing a Jagged Crescent smuggler could be fun).<br /> <br /> Underlying that difference is that I want humans, not monsters, to be responsible for the Conspiracies crimes. TF:V murders Network Zero Hunters in cold blood because they threaten America's ecconomic interests with those inconvinient truths; not because vampires are worried about being outed on youtube.<br /> <br /> And where did I or anyone say there's only one style of play for kiling monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, do you honestly expect that EVERY player will simply turn a blind eye to a superior officer who performs actions they strongly disagree with, or in some cases overtly breaks the ideals or statues of their organization? If you have that sort of overt corruption, SOME players are going to put the purity of the cause before following orders. If players want that sort of path, then it should be covered.<br /> <br /> And I can see where you're coming from with regards to &quot;humans being the ones culpable&quot;, but I don't see how having a couple plotlines with a &quot;cancer cell&quot; in an overall human-run organization detracts from that. If you want to crank up the irony, you could even have the &quot;cancer cell&quot; actually be one of the more ethical cells that might help the players shut down the corrupt cells. The top is still human, and still calling out the hits on other conspiracies.<br /> <br /> In general, I'd just like an expansion of the Gray On Gray on Black Morality and the incomprehensibility of who is really loyal to what or what right even is. <br /> <br /> To this end, I rather like pushing the conspiracy versus conspiracy conflicts on the one hand, and playing up the notion of potential monster allies on the other, in coordination with an untrustworthy home base. In Mortal Remains, particularly, some of the &quot;monster&quot; types like Geist or Changeling are all but openly treated as allies by some compacts or conspiracies. (Network Zero letting itself get used to pass messages from the dead by Geists...) Les Mysteres overtly has calling spirits as its main weapon.<br /> <br /> Allies have a tendency of dragging allies into wars not of their own choosing. If we use VALKYRIE as a metaphor for US Military interventionism, how often have dictators been supported because we hated some enemy of that dictator more? VALKYRIE goes in to prop up a vampire prince against the werewolves pounding at its door that the brass sees as a greater threat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:36:33-08:00","id":422708,"title":"","content":"The issue is thematic focus. The game promises monster hunters on the front cover and so the focus should be on monsters, not your own Conspiracy or other Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> Of course I don't expect every player to turn a blind eye to a superior officer they disagree with; that would be nonsense. However the books can still focus on Ascending Ones hunting monsters and not playing politics to ween their Conspiracy away from drug money. Even though other Hunters absolutely will fight the Ascending Ones because &quot;Elixirs are filthy witchcraft&quot; that doesn't need to be given as much word count as fighting actual witches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=422388#post422388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and playing up the notion of potential monster allies on the other</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with that. Hunting doesn't have to mean killing, you can go &quot;bargain hunting&quot; at the Goblin Market for example.<br /> <br /> So long as the Hunters are portrayed as humans who make alliances with the supernatural because it advances their own interests I have zero problems. Have a look at Dream Catchers in my sig, I wrote the Office of the Lord Stewards. A diplomatic Hunter Conspiracy who have absolutely no combat experience whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T04:34:59-08:00","id":422809,"title":"","content":"I see little reason they couldn't do both - Hunter already addresses internal problems and politicking to some level of depth without sacrificing the procedural hunting of external adversaries; with the much more concise writing style we've seen adopted as per Blood &amp; Smoke (hopefully WoD 2nd is rewritten in part with that voice; it really beats the generic vague nonsensical pontificating filler that 40% of WW books are devoted to) they'll have plenty of room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:02:10-08:00","id":423201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=422708#post422708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is thematic focus. The game promises monster hunters on the front cover and so the focus should be on monsters, not your own Conspiracy or other Conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, look at VASCU, then. It's a branch of the FBI dedicated specifically to hunting &quot;humans&quot; in the form of slashers, not &quot;monsters&quot;, at least in the sense of protagonists of the other game lines. You could say that they're still hunting &quot;monsters&quot; because they're hunting humans that have forsaken their humanity towards a relentless expression of violence towards the world around them... but again, wasn't the whole theme of Hunter that you become the monster, too? <br /> <br /> I don't think it needs equal wordcount or anything, but having a few bits in there to talk about hunting the monsters of another or even your own conspiracy is something that hammers home that &quot;Those Who Hunt Monsters&quot; conceit that really is the core theme of the game. I mean, reading over Horror Recognition Guide, there was one chapter where the guy was talking about how only those psychos would just up and torch the cat lady's place... and then when he found out about what the cats were, he went and torched the cat lady's place. Block by Bloody Block basically puts some compacts in different blocks as being as explicitly villains as the other monsters, with Ashwood Abbey being a major potential antagonist. <br /> <br /> And I mean, come on, some of these conspiracies, especially Cheiron, just beg for a plotline that goes, &quot;Well, we were playing with werewolf and promethian body parts on spirit-ridden test subjects, and - OOPSIES! - we accidentally made an unstoppable Ouroboric abomination that continues to grow in power and size as it consumes the flesh and souls of everything in its path. We've got orders you have to work overtime on your kid's birthday to be cannonfodder for the beast while we figure out what it's made of to get a hint as to what the thing is weak to. Meanwhile, just know that fire and bullets do nothing. Oh, and the research director seems to have called it his &quot;child&quot; before merging and is now the lead sentience of it, so tell him we're regretfully going to have to ask for his resignation before it swallows you -- I mean IF it swallows you -- I mean, I'm sure you'll be fine -- just tell him to please remember he's not a god and to ask him to nicely compress himself into a study pin without killing him, 'k?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:23:49-08:00","id":423299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=423201#post423201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, look at VASCU, then. It's a branch of the FBI dedicated specifically to hunting &quot;humans&quot; in the form of slashers, not &quot;monsters&quot;, at least in the sense of protagonists of the other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider Slasher's to be &quot;monsters&quot;, Rippers fall into a grey area for sure (which is why it's a very <i>good</i> thing that VASCU needs to give them a fair trial) but Scourges are supernatural and outright evil.<br /> <br /> But definitions are vague.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=423201#post423201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wasn't the whole theme of Hunter that you become the monster, too?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. That's like saying the whole theme of hunter is getting killed by monsters, or the whole theme of Promethian is to fail your pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Lots of hunters get killed by monsters, lots of hunters become a monster or at least fall into a grey area, most Promethians never become human. I wouldn't say any of them is the theme or the core of the game.<br /> <br /> And that's really the crux of our disagreement. I don't deny that these things are part of hunter, but I don't consider them to be the core and I don't think they should be the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:04:16-08:00","id":423346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=423299#post423299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. That's like saying the whole theme of hunter is getting killed by monsters, or the whole theme of Promethian is to fail your pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Lots of hunters get killed by monsters, lots of hunters become a monster or at least fall into a grey area, most Promethians never become human. I wouldn't say any of them is the theme or the core of the game.<br /> <br /> And that's really the crux of our disagreement. I don't deny that these things are part of hunter, but I don't consider them to be the core and I don't think they should be the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, poor wording, but the <i>THREAT</i> of becoming a monster is a core part of the game. The <i>THREAT</i> of how real the possibility of failing to become human is a very real shadow over every Promethian's shoulder. The <i>THREAT</i> of becoming worse than the monsters you hunt is a core theme in the game. Just like the <i>THREAT</i> of getting ripped apart by monsters, or letting the monsters kill another innocent while you dither around for your wishy-washy &quot;proof he's a monster&quot; is also the always-present doubt driving the hunter to more extreme leaps in judgement out of fear of what those monsters will do <i>if you don't stop them RIGHT NOW!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:08:36-08:00","id":423349,"title":"","content":"Threat I can get behind, portray it like the threat of a Promethian failing their pilgramage.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I think that's about the same as it's handled in 1e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:50:00-08:00","id":425741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=423349#post423349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threat I can get behind, portray it like the threat of a Promethian failing their pilgramage.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I think that's about the same as it's handled in 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I never meant that those things were different from 1e.<br /> <br /> Rather, I like a lot of what 1e did with the existing compacts and conspiracies, and would like to continue seeing the hunt, but that the game could be made more thematically paranoid and unsure. What you have in 1e is &quot;There's a werewolf! Let's shoot it!&quot; where a lot of hunters take a rather gung-ho take on the Vigil. The main threat being that of the monsters not really being monsters. (Whether that means mundane human or actually a &quot;monster&quot; that was a law-abiding citizen that actually hunted down only rampaging spirits and genuinely was a net benefit to society.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to see more work/text shown towards the interactions with &quot;monsters&quot; that aren't shooting the various other denizens of darkness, while also playing up the clandestine rivalries between the conspiracies and compacts, themselves. (Especially since many compacts and conspiracies are filled with &quot;monsters&quot; of their own... Even beyond Cheiron, there's a group of cannibals that eat witches so that they can become witches. How is that NOT monsterous? On the Vigil's radar, doesn't a &quot;human&quot; that got a witch's power through eating the witch sound exactly like a witch, anyway?)<br /> <br /> Besides that, different conspiracies and compacts are clearly geared more towards specific supernaturals than others, and because of their differing motivations for their hunts, are more-or-less willing to live and let live or even covertly ally themselves with different creatures that could put them into open conflict with the conspiracies that hunt their allies, even if only by mistaken association. (VALKYRIE agents passing off forged documents to changelings to keep a source planted close to a court gets jumped by Long Night hunters who just assumed anyone willingly helping the demons must also be a demon or at least worthy of death.)<br /> <br /> Basically, Hunters frequently try to look at their world in black-and-white terms when it's really gray. I'm saying to play up the gray. The moral doubts pop up occasionally in the little sidebars or small story hook blurbs, but they're not present in the main text, itself. It's &quot;witches are EEEEEEVIL! Burn the witch!&quot; throughout the main thrust of most of what's in the book.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, while perhaps moving a little in the other direction, I'd like it if some of the compacts weren't so clearly Too Dumb To Live. Null Mysteriis is especially flagrant, as it represents people trying to approach the supernatural with a rational mindset, and instead they come off as strawman take-that's at how scientists are stupid. Les Mysteres are almost an insult to a wide host of religions, since they are basically taking a whole range of faiths, and the general implication is that they're all just going to get spirit-ridden until spirit-claimed, as well as that the spirits they believe in are basically just parasitic, and creating those religions to throw their followers as cannon fodder at werewolves. Other groups that seem more like a cartoonish parody of a group of people than actually developed characters include Network Zero, Ashwood Abbey, and Keepers of the Source. I could also make an argument about Cheiron, Hunt Club, or Long Night, but you could kind of make the argument there are certainly institutions like them. It still opens the question of how many people play a game of Cheiron for the &quot;horror&quot;, and how many play it as Paranoia set in nWoD?<br /> <br /> I mean, to go back to Null Mysteriis, the concept of a scientist trying to make sense of these things that clearly are out there is compelling, but it's presented to players with vignettes that basically go, &quot;HI THERE, MR VAMPIRE! I'M ACTIVELY BLOWING YOUR MASQUERADE, AND I'M GOING TO GO OVER INTO THAT DARK CORNER OVER THERE AND INVITE YOU TO HAVE A BIG DISCUSSION WITH ME, AND OH GOSH, IF YOU'D BE SO NICE, TRY NOT TO MURDER ME TOO HARD!&quot; Even when they tried to break that mold, they only wound up making them Cheiron with a fresh coat of paint - psychopaths with scalpels that ripped people apart for &quot;SCIENCE!&quot; Surely, there's something besides Lois Lane or Dr. Mangele they can be modeled after...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 03-04-2015, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:25:10-08:00","id":425758,"title":"","content":"You know, part of me wonders if it would be better if Hunter was its own gameline, separate from the NWoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:59:04-08:00","id":426024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=425758#post425758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, part of me wonders if it would be better if Hunter was its own gameline, separate from the NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Delta Green</i> might be right up your alley. Basically imagine a Compact getting its own entire book, and replacing the monsters of the nWoD with the Cthulhu Mythos. It adds other international Compacts as well, along with several antagonist groups. Think about what the step between The Union and VALYRIE (without their toys) would be, and you're right on the mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T02:51:16-08:00","id":426347,"title":"","content":"There's also the excellent Monster of the Week. Hunter thrives in that peculiar White Wolf cross between modern horror and urban fantasy, where most horror settings the monsters tend to be more phenomena than characters, less organized and institutional, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T00:59:00-07:00","id":435448,"title":"","content":"What I want to see from Hunter 2ed is the following... <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Hunter Needs a Focused Theme</b> - Vampire must feed, Werewolves must hunt, so what defines Hunter as a theme?<br /> <br /> My pick would be that Hunters must endure. (Your pick could be different but still, please, pick one thing and make it awesome)<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>Building on that Theme</b> - What does enduring mean in regards to the Vigil and the greater game focus?<br /> <br /> It means that Hunters, differing from regular humans, don't turn away from the horror or their fates. It means, Hunters as characters are going to die. Often in heroic and tragic ways and often in terms of your counting the days till shit slips up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>Story Progression and Mechanics Integration </b>- What needs to be in 2ed to support this theme?<br /> <br /> Alternate XP system. If you have a character possibly dying, how can the next character step in and fill their shoes? Possibly something like the Sanctity of Merits but for Cells or Compacts or Conspiracies. Touchstones become the next line of Hunters. Storytelling and filling in downtime should also support this, because it takes time to fill in lost shoes.<br /> <br /> Very simple (and fun) character creation. If Hunter goes this route and shows off just how fragile and deadly humanity is against the horrors, it should be a fun system and a quick one with lots of examples of how to transition and carry over what you loved about one character into another one.<br /> <br /> Progression for the party, not the character. This ties into the alternate XP system. What you buy in terms of Skills, Attributes etc, should get worked into the next character or the Cell as a whole. Special Hunter Merits should persist and provide growing bonuses, stories should build towards resolutions not for just one or a few characters but the Cell. Emphasis on the story of the Cell as one shared character that literally has separate ''cells&quot; of characters to support.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>Killing Muthaf*cking Monsers</b> - Hunter needs to be able to cross-over, and they need to be able to win.<br /> <br /> Hunters are the bane of every other game line. They are the big ball of humanity that you threaten people with in those games. Make that ball here and build it with some really nasty toys. Show just how effective regular human beings can be at controlling their environment or settling scores or just being badasses.<br /> <br /> Badass normal should be a trope in Hunter, it should something that is costly or grows from the forces of many. Humanity has numbers and cooperation. Cells have each other. Human spirit needs to be able to win out in the end or wither and die tragically. Equipment, Merits, Powers, Tactics etc. They need to support this. Things should suck if they fail, but be amazing if they succeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>Dying like Weaksauce Mortals</b> - Don't contradict the other game lines.<br /> <br /> Humans are the fodder and chaff of every other game line. They are a resource or food or fodder or many other disposable things to the supernatural forces of the world. Every game line has ways to control them to their ends. Make it another cornerstone point of Hunter. You are facing something greater than yourself, and possibly risking those you love.<br /> <br /> It needs to be implicit that death (or worse) is a very real possibility and that this is okay in Hunter. It's encouraged. It adds to the game and isn't punished because in the established World of Darkness narrative, its how things eventually go down for human beings. Maybe you change, you become the 'other' and that can be explored slightly in Hunter, but if you really want that go play one of the other game lines. Hunters die, go crazy or worse.<br /> <br /> Maybe your the one Cell who is crazy careful, and is losing touch with their own humanity. That should also get focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>License to Print Monsters</b> - What Storytellers need to explore other things that Hunters hunt.<br /> <br /> We need simple to use mechanics that interact with Conditions and Tilts that can build really cool and scary things. Broad powers with many possible outcomes that have a firm Storyteller only stamp on them. Something that is not unlike Influence for Spirits but a bit more detailed. Shadow creatures have shadow powers that cause fear of darkness. Fear creatures just cause fear outright or phobias. Same power, different themes etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /></li> <li><b>Maybe Custom Powers</b> - It's not what I expect out of Hunter...<br /> <br /> ...but you do a good job of it with Mage, maybe something toned for Hunter could do? I don't really mind but it would make a lot of players happy.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> That's what I want to see out of 2ed Hunter.<br /> <br /> Firm supported theme, focus on group progression rather than character progression, highlighting humanity as both awesome and frail, cool toys and custom monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-10-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:36:23-07:00","id":438325,"title":"","content":"I know this might not be popular, but for my own table, and what I'd do if I was designing the setting, I'd drop the Cainite Heresy as a distinct Conspiracy, and harvest its coolest elements for Malleus Maleficarum - specifically have Malleus have originated in a vampire ruled ghoul-cult (via vitea-tainted communion wine) that rebelled in the early 16th Century, hence the Ghoul Cardinal still at its head, and harvest the Rites of Denial for &quot;Benediction&quot; (keep the Catholic names and prayers, but have them work through sanctified blood - that being a controlled resource and the dark nature there of actually makes it make in-setting sense that Malleus keeps their powers so secret, rather than the Church resurrecting the dead left-and-right).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:19:37-07:00","id":438707,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's going to be popular. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It takes out the Cainites who're just awesome. It makes it impossible to play a genuine god powered Catholic hunter; which is a very powerful archetype.<br /> <br /> For why the Church hides Benedictions, here's what I have. If they did the reaction would be divided into three groups:<br /> <br /> 1) Genuine open minded skeptics (think Null Mysteriis) who'd say &quot;yes that's very impressive, but how do I know it's God and not just witchcraft? I'd like to learn how to do it though&quot;<br /> 2) The average WoD mortal who's petrified of the supernatural and would flee from the Church.<br /> 3) People who would become genuine believers in response. This group is smaller than #2 and most of them are in Church anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:29:46-07:00","id":439240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=438707#post438707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's going to be popular. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It takes out the Cainites who're just awesome. It makes it impossible to play a genuine god powered Catholic hunter; which is a very powerful archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally think &quot;genuine God powered&quot; is a thing that should absolutely not exist in the World of Darkness. Things that LOOK LIKE THAT, or are BELIEVED TO BE THAT BY ITS WIELDER - sure. But the genuine article, absolutely not. I mean, I can headcanon what Spirits are actually behind Benedictions - and I have - but canon needs to do more to undermine or explore that point.<br /> <br /> As to your reasons why, I have to disagree - if the Catholic Church had real miracles like Benedictions at their disposal they'd be the One World Religion. At least the way they're presented in canon that just handwaves how they're studied, discovered, why Malleus has a monopoly on them...<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally I don't find that Cainites that cool as a complete picture - their coolest elements are their backstory and their blood rituals, which are harvestable to fill in the blanks for Malleus at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:52:36-07:00","id":439256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439240#post439240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally think &quot;genuine God powered&quot; is a thing that should absolutely not exist in the World of Darkness. Things that LOOK LIKE THAT, or are BELIEVED TO BE THAT BY ITS WIELDER - sure. But the genuine article, absolutely not. I mean, I can headcanon what Spirits are actually behind Benedictions - and I have - but canon needs to do more to undermine or explore that point.<br /> <br /> As to your reasons why, I have to disagree - if the Catholic Church had real miracles like Benedictions at their disposal they'd be the One World Religion. At least the way they're presented in canon that just handwaves how they're studied, discovered, why Malleus has a monopoly on them...<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally I don't find that Cainites that cool as a complete picture - their coolest elements are their backstory and their blood rituals, which are harvestable to fill in the blanks for Malleus at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the implications in the Dark Era, and what we know of the world of darkness, it makes perfect sense that they don't show Benedictions to the public. It'd traumatize them, and the legitimacy of them would be questioned. The legitimacy of the &quot;divine&quot; nature of Benedictions has been questioned from the get-go, and from what we know of the Cardinal in charge, he also has a shady past, and I bet operating on the tier he does, he probably knows a bit more than Joe Schmoe Malleus about what the Benedictions <i>actually </i>are, and I'm sure he's very keen on not inviting anyone's scrutiny deeper into their nature in addition to their Vigil.<br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr, we don't know if it's really from God, and the head of the Conspiracy almost definitely has a better idea about that, he's likely to be the biggest voice behind keeping it quiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T20:25:07-07:00","id":439294,"title":"","content":"I would feel a lot better about Benedictions honestly if they were treated as the plot hook they should be (some history about where they came from, how Malleus came to wield them, etc) instead of just handwaved magic powers to fit a niche.<br /> <br /> For example, did they exist before Malleus did? Why does Malleus have monopoly on them? Are they studied out of secret tomes that Malleus alone possesses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:33:23-07:00","id":439502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439240#post439240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally think &quot;genuine God powered&quot; is a thing that should absolutely not exist in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. I wouldn't want to say explicitly that a god powered magic is the real deal; but leaving it open so that they might be - sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439240#post439240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IAs to your reasons why, I have to disagree - if the Catholic Church had real miracles like Benedictions at their disposal they'd be the One World Religion. At least the way they're presented in canon that just handwaves how they're studied, discovered, why Malleus has a monopoly on them...</div> </div> </div> </div> In the real world sure; but WoD people think differently about magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439240#post439240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IGenerally I don't find that Cainites that cool as a complete picture - their coolest elements are their backstory and their blood rituals, which are harvestable to fill in the blanks for Malleus at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the coolest elements is how they're a thematic foil to vampires. Their power comes from being small invisible groups and willing to self sacrafice. Constrast to a vampire who builds a big empire of pawns to keep themselves safe.<br /> <br /> The Catholic Church couldn't hit that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:34:21-07:00","id":439503,"title":"","content":"To elaborate on something that glamourweaver said: nowhere in the World of Darkness is there any incontestable <i>proof</i> of there being a benevolent God. Things like Benedictions can be cited as evidence of such a thing by those already inclined to believe; but it\u2019s <i>still</i> just a matter of faith. <br /> <br /> Also, Benedictions and Castigations need some revision in 2e, owing to Integrity not being Morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:46:59-07:00","id":439528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439256#post439256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr, we don't know if it's really from God, and the head of the Conspiracy almost definitely has a better idea about that, he's likely to be the biggest voice behind keeping it quiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it is from &quot;on high&quot;, Benedictions have been bolted onto an organization engaged in atrocities throughout it's history.<br /> <br /> &quot;Miracles are real!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Holy shit! WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING WITH THEM?!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:48:58-07:00","id":439532,"title":"","content":"Personally my idea of the WoD god is a well meaning Deity who's gotten promoted beyond his competence. The Peter Principle in effect.<br /> <br /> He's basically the god of desert dwelling nomads. He understands about protecting his chosen people from bandits, from diseases, and making sure their crops and flocks are healthy enough to feed the tribes.<br /> <br /> Basically he's like an uneducated peasant who's son went of to university. He's very proud, but when his son comes back to ask for advice about problems he's having in the city or for help with his philosophy dissertation god has zero clue what to do. I imagine him watching a bunch of Rabbi's or Cardinals debating theology and alternating between thinking &quot;how wonderful to have such smart children&quot; and &quot;I wish someone's sheep would get sick, then I'd be useful&quot;.<br /> <br /> Power wise he's roughly equivalent to things like Gaia, or the Hindu Pathenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:52:46-07:00","id":439535,"title":"","content":"Frankly, the fact that it\u2019s the World of <i>Darkness</i> makes including a provable benevolent higher power in the setting problematic, to say the least. The \u201cPeter Principle\u201d notion is more suitable to Scion than to the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-13-2015, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:10:31-07:00","id":439540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439502#post439502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the real world sure; but WoD people think differently about magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't - if you need to rewrite human nature to make your setting work, there is something wrong with your setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah, the coolest elements is how they're a thematic foil to vampires. Their power comes from being small invisible groups and willing to self sacrafice. Constrast to a vampire who builds a big empire of pawns to keep themselves safe. </div> </div> </div>You get that better with Tiers 1 &amp; 2 than a Tier 3 group is capable of delivering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:23:52-07:00","id":439548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439540#post439540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They shouldn't - if you need to rewrite human nature to make your setting work, there is something wrong with your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to David Brookshaw. In the World of Darkness, most people are Sleepers \u2014 that is, they\u2019re infected by a supernatural curse that influences them to turn away from the supernatural. It\u2019s at its most intense when you\u2019re dealing with Supernal magic; but it applies to a lesser degree to <i>all</i> kinds of supernatural phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:43:36-07:00","id":439585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439548#post439548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell that to David Brookshaw. In the World of Darkness, most people are Sleepers \u2014 that is, they\u2019re infected by a supernatural curse that influences them to turn away from the supernatural. It\u2019s at its most intense when you\u2019re dealing with Supernal magic; but it applies to a lesser degree to <i>all</i> kinds of supernatural phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the perspective of the Mage gameline, that's understandable. From the perspective of mortals and Hunters where you are asked &quot;What kind of weird thing happened in your past that you shrugged off/take note?&quot; as an inclusion of a character concept, it becomes problematic.<br /> <br /> Always found it more believable that Mortals stumble into strange stuff all the time (Hollows, verges, God-Machine projects) only to come running back to the safety of the familiar rather than hard coding it so that anything remotely supernatural attracts the attention of the Lie.<br /> <br /> If that was true, Arisen cults would have a hard time operating.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:17:35-07:00","id":439639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439548#post439548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell that to David Brookshaw. In the World of Darkness, most people are Sleepers \u2014 that is, they\u2019re infected by a supernatural curse that influences them to turn away from the supernatural. It\u2019s at its most intense when you\u2019re dealing with Supernal magic; but it applies to a lesser degree to <i>all</i> kinds of supernatural phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without Mage - the God Machine Rules update does make it very clear that most mortals have first hand experience with the supernatural but supress the memory. That's a major psychological difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:50:34-07:00","id":439670,"title":"","content":"Considering that benedictions don't prove anything, since you don't have to be priest, be a christian (a hunter can go and join the shamans of the cheval and keep their benedictions after all), or even remotely a good person (since slashers can use benedictions too), there is nothing problematic about benedictions existence. <br /> <br /> Nor is it a major advantage to the catholic church, since oh great, the catholic church has teachable magical powers. This is the world of darkness, so do the houngans, shaman, taoists, wiccans, druids, hermetics, hindu, worshippers of the greek gods, worshippers of the egyptian gods, and every other religion since the dawn of time. <br /> <br /> The only thing odd about the catholic church and its benedictions is that they use them to hunt monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:01:01-07:00","id":439671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439585#post439585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of the Mage gameline, that's understandable. From the perspective of mortals and Hunters where you are asked &quot;What kind of weird thing happened in your past that you shrugged off/take note?&quot; as an inclusion of a character concept, it becomes problematic.<br /> Always found it more believable that Mortals stumble into strange stuff all the time (Hollows, verges, God-Machine projects) only to come running back to the safety of the familiar rather than hard coding it so that anything remotely supernatural attracts the attention of the Lie.<br /> If that was true, Arisen cults would have a hard time operating.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fact in the NWOD that mortals do not think the way we do when it comes to the supernatural. Whether this is the result of the Sleeping Curse is up in the air (pretty sure DaveB said this himself actually). .<br /> <br /> Really though, when you have a setting that's as bursting at the seams with wierdness as the NWOD, you kind of need something like that to maintain plausiblity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:57:55-07:00","id":439701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439585#post439585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the perspective of the Mage gameline, that's understandable. From the perspective of mortals and Hunters where you are asked &quot;What kind of weird thing happened in your past that you shrugged off/take note?&quot; as an inclusion of a character concept, it becomes problematic.<br /> <br /> Always found it more believable that Mortals stumble into strange stuff all the time (Hollows, verges, God-Machine projects) only to come running back to the safety of the familiar rather than hard coding it so that anything remotely supernatural attracts the attention of the Lie.<br /> <br /> If that was true, Arisen cults would have a hard time operating.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As others have noted, this isn't a <b>Mage</b> thing, it's a <b>World of Darkness</b> thing - people know, deep down, that there's something wrong with the world they're living in and turn away from it. It's built into the nWoD as a setting, and gets clearly stated in Innocents, God-Machine Chronicle, and even Hunter itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:04:31-07:00","id":439707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=439701#post439701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and even Hunter itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know the Union's write up in Compacts and Conspiracies talks about it. Is there any other points where it comes up?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:16:50-07:00","id":439944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=438707#post438707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For why the Church hides Benedictions, here's what I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also add that God gave them these powers for a reason, and that reason is not advertising.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Tier question, Tiers have only made an appearance in 2nd edition in the God Machine chronicles, where they've been defined pretty much as &quot;What's at stake.&quot; That's a pretty good definition for Hunter too, so I'd now advocate leaving Tiers at that, and making the other parts of the concept to a set of dichotomies:<br /> <br /> <b>Cell vs Compact:</b> Is it just you, your ovaries, a couple of bffs and whatever weapons you can scrape together? Or are you part of a bigger group that provides context for both the monsters and the Vigil, at the cost of having bosses to tell you what to do?<br /> (Different groups will vary in how much context they offer, and in how rigid their orders, but I've cooled off thinking there's a point to mechanically differenting them over that).<br /> <br /> <b>Visceral vs Cinematic:</b> Visceral means you can risk Willpower, but otherwise you're stuck as a normal human. Cinematic opens up options like the Compact Endowments from C&amp;C - Unearthed Secrets, Prayer, All Seeing Eye, and I'm Doing Science are apt for this.<br /> (You <i>could</i> break it into three, with a lower level unable to risk Willpower either).<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane vs Empowered:</b> Are you limited to mundane traits and Merits, with perhaps some of the mortal-only supernatural options? Or have you discovered supernatural techniques - ie the conspiracy Endowments?<br /> <br /> <b>Lone vs Connected:</b> Is your group on its own, in which case you're limited to who you know through your ordinary life? Or does it have ties to useful mundanes or other groups like itself? The latter opens up options like Friends and Neighbours from the Union's C&amp;C chapter - which can easily be repurposed to other strata of society.<br /> <br /> Most organisations could be primarily written from the perspective of &quot;compact/visceral/mundane/lone&quot; - but where appropriate add sections asking:<br /> What if it's just a cell? (VASCU as an agent or two in the basement, demonic progeny who haven't been recruited by Lady Lucie - for the Union, this might be the default, as it's more cells that have found out about each other than a firm organisation)<br /> What if it's cinematic? (Offers one or more cinematic options suited to the group - either the Long Night or the Malleus can draw strength from shared prayer, Null Mysteriis can do their science, and the Cherion group certainly has people who can - for thrill seekers like the Bear Lodge, this might be the default),<br /> What if it's empowered? (Suggests a full-on Endowment - Ashwood Abbey have done enough drugs that they could have found Elixirs they can use, while Null Mysteriis could puzzle out Advanced Armoury - for the Lucifuge and their Castigation, this would be the default)<br /> What if it's connected? (Any of these groups could draw on people from their spheres to help them - for some, like the Barrett Commission or Malleus Maleficarum, it could be the default).<br /> And finally, which type of monster is most likely to have taken it over, and why?<br /> <br /> Depending on how many groups could be fit into the space, alongside the big twelve, I wouldn't mind seeing VASCU, the Barret Commission, the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, Habibi Ma, the Bear Lodge, and Les Mysteres (as a more specifically Afro-Caribbean group). Ones of the big twelve I wouldn't mind seeing dropped to make room are Ashwood Abbey (in favour of the Bear Lodge) and Network Zero.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the &quot;central conflict&quot; - the analogue of the Strix, Idigam, Fallen World, and Firestorms - I'd go with a question, how far outside the human world are you willing to go? Endowments are most obvious aspect of this, including Castigation which denies the choice was really there to start with. But the cinematic options I mentioned can be cast in that light - their abilities are an easy way to start seeing yourself as better than other people. And the connections can too - how much are you willing to use bystanders as tools in the Vigil, and how different is that from monsters use innocents in their own schemes? And there's the Code of course, though that would need revamping in the face of Integrity's greater variation over Morality.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding inspirational material, Dracula's way more of a Hunter novel than a Vampire novel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:02:36-07:00","id":440084,"title":"","content":"First thing is the theme in my opinion. Vampire must Feed, Werewolf must Hunt, etc. Hunter must Protect or Hunter must survive. HtV 2e just needs to be a bit different... it needs less vampires and mummies, and more... well Slender man, Death's Pass incident, mothman, SCP Foundation... definitely SCP. Compacts and conspiracies are OK. They just need slight adjusting. Again, check SCP groups of interest...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:08:22-07:00","id":440094,"title":"","content":"It's like people have missed out on that wonderful little word Vigil.<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what a hunter does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:11:27-07:00","id":440097,"title":"","content":"Hunter has always operated on the assumption that the various supernatural Masquerades, regardless of the amount of crossover with the other gamelines, strongly rely on the tendency among humans to ignore and rationalize the supernatural. On a subconscious level, humans simply don't want to believe it exists. Hunters are those few who either choose to believe, or are forced into it.<br /> <br /> What keeps emerging from the discussion is, I think, that Hunter covers a wide range of stories even by World of Darkness standards, and it has to support them somehow. Tiers are a way to do it, but they need to be contextualized differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:21:35-07:00","id":440108,"title":"","content":"By the way, there's an entire argument between Raven and myself about why Benedictions aren't used in public. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions\">Make of it what you will.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:24:27-07:00","id":440110,"title":"","content":"I didn't had any problems with tiers in my chronicles. The game should always be about horror, cause that's what matters. Whether your girlfriend and sister watched some weird tape, or an episode of a show that doesn't exist, and now something is after them, or the population of an entire town by the lake vanished without a trace, and there are strange oil marks around the pipes and drains, it shouldn't matter whether its local or global... its about Survival...<br /> Sorry 'bout the long description, but I don't see problem with tiers... But there should be more WEIRD and BATS**T scary...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:03:00-07:00","id":440268,"title":"","content":"This may not be a very popular idea, but I'd like to actually see Hunter as both a minor template and a major template or series of major templates for some of the more supernaturally-juiced Conspiracies like Cheiron Group, Lucifuge, etc., supporting the whole &quot;He who fights monsters should see to it that he does not become one&quot; schtick. Maybe have corrupted Hunters of various stripes (Enfants Terribles, rogue Cheiron employees with more after-market parts than stock...) as major gameline-specific adversaries to supplement the Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and whatnot.<br /> <br /> More God-Machine. Specifically, tying the line a little bit more closely to the God-Machine Chronicles setting in terms of &quot;GMC is the default setting and gives you the rules for creating ordinary mortals; Hunter gives you the toolkit to roll up someone with more punch, plus quick and dirty stats for the splats from other gamelines so you can fight them. Now here's some further background on the GMC setting.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-13-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:34:19-07:00","id":440302,"title":"","content":"I could get behind the idea of certain groups having a low scale supernatural merit as part of their shindig. Cheiron I'd mandate you'd need a certain number of Thaumatech before that happens but-Hmm, ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:40:23-07:00","id":440529,"title":"","content":"I could imagine a Merit that gives certain Hunters a Supernatural Tolerance for the purpose of resisting powers <i>only</i>. I am specifically not talking about Conviction or an equivalent trait, but a Merit representing supernatural protection (like Infernal heritage, having imbibed a powerful Elixir, being loaded with Thaumatech, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:43:08-07:00","id":440531,"title":"","content":"As far as <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s monsters go, I could see doing one of two things: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Double down on the \u201chunters fight approximations of the other gamelines\u201d model, with the Antagonists section including <b>Mortal Remains</b>-esque monster templates for each supernatural gameline. <br /> \u2022 Downplay the \u201capproximations of other gamelines\u201d angle, and instead focus on Outsiders: monsters who <i>don\u2019t</i> fit even the rou outlines of the other gamelines. <br /> <br /> Personally, I want to see both featured somewhere with <b>Hunter 2e</b> taking one approach and <b>WoD 2e</b> taking the other. With this in mind, I\u2019d rather <b>Hunter 2e</b> focus on the former approach while <b>WoD 2e</b> focuses on the latter approach. But then, I\u2019d also rather <i>not</i> have WoD 2e feature the God-Machine Chronicle; that\u2019s already a standalone product that\u2019s virtually guaranteed to be 2e-compatible, and anyway the God-Machine is more suited to <b>Demon: the Descent</b> than as a central feature of the \u201cblue book\u201d line. Instead, I\u2019d rather <b>WoD 2e</b> feature an Outsiders Chronicle, with a focus on the fringes, as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:57:43-07:00","id":440546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=440531#post440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, I\u2019d rather <b>WoD 2e</b> feature an Outsiders Chronicle, with a focus on the fringes, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the specific reason why they went with the God-Machine instead of Outsiders is that Outsiders in general do not lend themselves well to ongoing stories and are more &quot;monster of the week&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:45:05-07:00","id":440626,"title":"","content":"I think that Hunters being inherently - that is, without requiring a merit - resistant to powers like the Sleeper Curse, Lunacy and such is something to be considered. Not as an inherent part of the gameline, but as an option for Storytellers to use. Perhaps as part of the 'heroic hunter' tier if that's what the game goes with. From a certain point of view, the Hunters' eyes are already open, or have been <i>torn </i>open; it's difficult to force them shut again. It doesn't fit every take on Hunter, of course. Which brings us back to there being several distinctive ways to run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:55:20-07:00","id":440638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=440626#post440626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Hunters being inherently - that is, without requiring a merit - resistant to powers like the Sleeper Curse, Lunacy and such is something to be considered. Not as an inherent part of the gameline, but as an option for Storytellers to use. Perhaps as part of the 'heroic hunter' tier if that's what the game goes with. From a certain point of view, the Hunters' eyes are already open, or have been <i>torn </i>open; it's difficult to force them shut again. It doesn't fit every take on Hunter, of course. Which brings us back to there being several distinctive ways to run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Armoury Reloaded had a good idea when it proposed the hack that being with your cell gave you increased resistance to Lunacy and Quiescence (which back then was possible to resist by anyone of high enough Willpower). Perhaps this system could be made a proper part of HtV. This would emphasize the &quot;strength in numbers&quot; aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:05:37-07:00","id":440646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=440546#post440546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the specific reason why they went with the God-Machine instead of Outsiders is that Outsiders in general do not lend themselves well to ongoing stories and are more \u201cmonster of the week\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda, yeah; but what\u2019s wrong with that? As I see it, that\u2019s one of the main differences between blue-book chronicles and Hunter chronicles: blue-book protagonists haven\u2019t taken up the Vigil; they\u2019re not out watching for the supernatural. Rather, they stumble over something in the dark that will likely kill em if they ignore it. So they deal with whatever monster has forced its way into their lives; and if they survive, they then go back to their regular lives. They <i>aren\u2019t</i> suited for ongoing stories, save only for those cases when the thing they initially stumble over ends up taking an ongoing story to overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:52:17-07:00","id":440681,"title":"","content":"Well, the point of GMC was to have a default Chronicle for mortals, which implies at least a certain degree of continuity. Consider how GMC talks a lot about ways to connect the various plot hooks in it, so that you can have a longer mortals chronicle with an overarching plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:42:30-07:00","id":441124,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, like in </span></span></span><i>Blood and Smoke</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> where you have a mask and dirge, maybe </span></span></span><i>Hunter</i> could reflect the meaning of a double life. A sort of &quot;person&quot; and &quot;calling&quot; division. The &quot;person&quot; highlights who a hunter is a a human being--their friends and family, their jobs and livelihoods, their hobbies and burdens (Perhaps you work as a tax accountant during the day, maybe even work at soup kitchens sometimes). Then you have the &quot;calling&quot;, which reflects the your personal vigil--which monsters you seek and why, as well as the organization which you associate with and why, and what your feelings are as a hunter (heading from the soup kitchen you torture a ghoul for the whereabouts of the vampire that controls him)...<br /> <br /> Also, each organization (compact, conspiracy, or other) could represent a certain theme in terms of the vigil. You carry a light in the vast expanse of darkness, you carry the vigil, and for what? Maybe you are in the Ashwood Abbey--which represents the idea of the THRILL of it--you have chosen to fight the darkness because you think it's great fun; because fighting overwhelming odds and facing horrors beyond you wildest imaginings is just your idea of a good time. Maybe you're in Task Force: Valkyrie--which stands for the idea of DUTY--you love your country, and you are duty bound to fight to protect it. Or, maybe you're in the Lucifuge--which represents the idea of CHOICE--you fight the darkness because you choose to. An act of ultimate defiance; destiny does not control you. The blood of the Devil might flow through your veins, but he doesn't own you--it's your choice. Or, maybe your in the Malleus Maleficarum--which represents FANATICISM--you slay monster because they <b>must be slain</b>. All the powers of Hell will fall like wheat before your Scythe, and you won't stop until they all burn in Hell!!! <br /> <br /> I also agree with others--endowments could work on all levels of organization. But, I might also like to see endowments divided into gifts and equipment (much like coils and scales were given to the Ordo Dracul in <i>Blood and Smoke</i>) so as to make things a bit more versatile. Like say for the Ascending Ones, you might have the gift of Elixirs (alchemically poisoned potions) which enhance the body for the hunt, but for equipment you might have alchemically treated swords or poisoned arrows. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T03:22:23-07:00","id":441144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=441124#post441124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, like in </span></span></span><i>Blood and Smoke</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> where you have a mask and dirge, maybe </span></span></span><i>Hunter</i> could reflect the meaning of a double life. A sort of &quot;person&quot; and &quot;calling&quot; division. The &quot;person&quot; highlights who a hunter is a a human being--their friends and family, their jobs and livelihoods, their hobbies and burdens (Perhaps you work as a tax accountant during the day, maybe even work at soup kitchens sometimes). Then you have the &quot;calling&quot;, which reflects the your personal vigil--which monsters you seek and why, as well as the organization which you associate with and why, and what your feelings are as a hunter (heading from the soup kitchen you torture a ghoul for the whereabouts of the vampire that controls him)...</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the idea of replacing Hunters' Virtue and Vice, I think it would send the wrong messages if mages get to keep Virtue and Vice, because they are the most human monsters, but Hunters <i>don't</i>. I could imagine a third Anchor trait exclusive to Hunters, though, which would fit in nicely since Hunters often live or die (literally) by their Willpower more so than many monsters. This trait should probably be related to the Vigil directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:26:57-07:00","id":441270,"title":"","content":"Instead of replacing Virtue/Vice, what they could do is in addition to the Profession merit you could take something that represented your &quot;style&quot; as a Hunter. They could even - dare I say it - call it a &quot;Creed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another idea that sort of manages the Lunacy/Quiescence issue (though Lunacy is fixed now) is just slap them with Conviction instead of Integrity. And like Harmony or Memory play with the system, I could see loss of Conviction risking dropping the character &quot;back into&quot; Integrity. So it more acts as a kind of buffer to weirdness and horror, letting the Hunter keep on the Vigil, rather than a full alternate morality (which would be weird since, y'know, people). But playing around with the morality systems seems like something they're willing to do these days. And an alternate morality scale doesn't really &quot;dehumanize&quot; them that much; Mages have Wisdom and are still people, Hunters could have Conviction and still be people. Integrity represents the theme of nWoD characters not necessarily experienced much with the supernatural trapped in a horror movie type one-off situation; Conviction represents the inner strength of will needed to then intentionally start diving into horror movie situations <i>on purpose</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:49:48-07:00","id":441604,"title":"","content":"In <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Werewolf</b>, Touchstones exist to pull you toward a certain \u201ckarmic trait\u201d extreme: High Humanity or Flesh/Spirit Harmony. In <b>Hunter 1e</b>, Professions were described as \u201cgrounding\u201d you and preventing you from becoming too much of a monster. IMHO, though, that never really worked. OTOH, I could see <b>Hunter 2e</b> protagonists getting Touchstones that work a lot like the ones in <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Werewolf</b>: some relationship with a person who is <i>not</i> involved in the Vigil that helps keep the hunter sane.<br /> <br /> As for Conviction, I still think that something like <b>Mirrors</b>\u2019 Conviction-as-a-power-stat would work best \u2014 on the condition that it be a strictly optional trait for those who like the idea of a scale measuring how devoted you are to the Vigil (just like 1e\u2019s Code was a strictly optional system for those who liked having a mechanism for immunizing hunters from certain repetitive Morality losses for a price).<br /> <br /> And speaking of the Code: that <i>is</i> <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s tweak to the \u201ckarmic trait\u201d; and it works quite well as written. The main thing I\u2019d change concerning it in 2e would be to adapt some of the psychotherapy rules from <b>Asylum</b> as a means of undoing the Code and bringing the hunter back to a more normal mindset. (Bear in mind that the Code itself is an adaptation of a system that first appeared in <b>Dogs of War</b>, as a way of describing how someone who shoots other people for a living could keep from dropping to low Morality.)<br /> <br /> Finally, I\u2019d want 2e\u2019s Aspirations to be supplemented by one or two Vigil-specific Aspirations that grant Practical Experience. <i>That</i> would be where your goals as a hunter play in, not as an Anchor \u2014 that is, it would be something that speeds character development, not something that generates Willpower or resists Integrity degeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-14-2015, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:36:14-07:00","id":441958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=440638#post440638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Armoury Reloaded had a good idea when it proposed the hack that being with your cell gave you increased resistance to Lunacy and Quiescence (which back then was possible to resist by anyone of high enough Willpower). Perhaps this system could be made a proper part of HtV. This would emphasize the &quot;strength in numbers&quot; aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that could work, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:01:30-07:00","id":441990,"title":"","content":"Lunacy already gives a \u201cstrength in numbers\u201d bonus to resisting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:29:28-07:00","id":442090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=440531#post440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s monsters go, I could see doing one of two things:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Double down on the \u201chunters fight approximations of the other gamelines\u201d model, with the Antagonists section including <b>Mortal Remains</b>-esque monster templates for each supernatural gameline.<br /> \u2022 Downplay the \u201capproximations of other gamelines\u201d angle, and instead focus on Outsiders: monsters who <i>don\u2019t</i> fit even the rou outlines of the other gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this brings me to my big issue concerning Hunter in general. I simply can't see how Hunter can be it's own game without stepping on toes if they used other splats with their full spectrum of abilities as actual antagonists. It's actually one of the reasons I've never liked seeing Hunter crossed with any other gameline, simply because some of the abilities and items introduced in Hunter compromised that system integrity of whatever it was crossed with, sometimes in ways that straight up shouldn't have worked going by the way the other splats abilities actually worked.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:24:25-07:00","id":443984,"title":"","content":"Well, Ashenrogue, I'd say that it's a mistake to limit hunter to hunting creatures straight out of the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Vampire has an entire book filled with alternate vampires, so if in a hunter game they come across vampires who are the result of a communicable disease, well, so what? <br /> <br /> Niche protection isn't a thing in the nwod, there are several types of vampires, werewolves, magicians, angels, demons, constructs, etc.<br /> <br /> Telling the difference between a shaman, a mage, a sorcerer, a thaumaturge, a son of phobos, and an occultist is kind of not the point of the vast majority of hunter games.<br /> <br /> In first ed vampire, anyway, a wooden bullet wouldn't stake a vampire, yet wooden bullets of vampire staking are a thing in hunter. Well, who says that the vampires it works against are kindred? <br /> <br /> The only issue you can't ignore like that, is one tactic off the top of my head, and that one less ignores the canon of another gameline but the basic canon that you can't get rid of major templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:09:51-07:00","id":444135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=441990#post441990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunacy already gives a \u201cstrength in numbers\u201d bonus to resisting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I guess it'd have to take another form, then. Or a cell of hunters could be treated as a bigger number of people than it actually is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=442090#post442090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this brings me to my big issue concerning Hunter in general. I simply can't see how Hunter can be it's own game without stepping on toes if they used other splats with their full spectrum of abilities as actual antagonists. It's actually one of the reasons I've never liked seeing Hunter crossed with any other gameline, simply because some of the abilities and items introduced in Hunter compromised that system integrity of whatever it was crossed with, sometimes in ways that straight up shouldn't have worked going by the way the other splats abilities actually worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got this complaint. If the abilities from Hunter that clash with other gamelines bother you, don't use them in crossover games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T14:59:31-07:00","id":444934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=443984#post443984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, Ashenrogue, I'd say that it's a mistake to limit hunter to hunting creatures straight out of the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Vampire has an entire book filled with alternate vampires, so if in a hunter game they come across vampires who are the result of a communicable disease, well, so what?<br /> <br /> Niche protection isn't a thing in the nwod, there are several types of vampires, werewolves, magicians, angels, demons, constructs, etc.<br /> <br /> Telling the difference between a shaman, a mage, a sorcerer, a thaumaturge, a son of phobos, and an occultist is kind of not the point of the vast majority of hunter games.<br /> <br /> In first ed vampire, anyway, a wooden bullet wouldn't stake a vampire, yet wooden bullets of vampire staking are a thing in hunter. Well, who says that the vampires it works against are kindred?<br /> <br /> The only issue you can't ignore like that, is one tactic off the top of my head, and that one less ignores the canon of another gameline but the basic canon that you can't get rid of major templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe my post wasn't really clear but what you mention is the issue I have with Hunter. Yes, you could say that they work on other things that are similar to but not the splats in question, sure. But when it comes down to actually having Hunter interact with the other gamelines things start to fall apart. To do what they do they can't really be involved with actual Kindred, or real Awakened, or genuine Uratha; they have to be off-brand knockoffs that kinda look like the real thing but aren't quite there.<br /> <br /> I've always had this feeling like Hunter isn't really a part of the world of darkness, but are in some parallel spin-off that has things kinda similar to the what is present in the main line but aren't really the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:28:18-07:00","id":445791,"title":"","content":"You can use them with the full splats from the other games just fine. It generally means that the other critters are more detailed and usually a little more powerful than their dread powered analogs, but it's nothing you can't manage with care. Occasionally you have to decide how a given Tactic or Endowment might interact, but again, nothing too difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:07:22-07:00","id":447187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/411243-what-do-you-want-from-a-second-edition?p=414791#post414791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe you're forgetting that there are two &quot;tribes&quot; in TF:V. The <i>Suits </i>and the <i>SWAT. </i>The SWAT guys are your paramilitary type that go in guns blazing and are all soldiers. Suits are more like FBI agents of the Supernatural; the MIB. They drive around in a black muscle car with a boot full of high-tech devices. One might indeed be a scientist and might have a portable lab of high-tech analysis equipment for quick sample analysis and ENE identification. Quite frankly, I always thought that the Suits felt more Hunter than the SWAT guys anyway. They always felt like foils and antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of like this idea. The players who have been studying the supernatural and trying to understand it and come to a safe way to deal with it and the paramilitary who go in and shoot first and ask questions later. It would be an interesting plot point to have the player play Suits, who have managed to broker a deal with, say a pack of werewolves, only to have the soldiers come in and bungle everything, slaughtering the pack, leaving a power vacuum. This of course causes spirits to come out of every nook and cranny, sliding out of the shadows, and perhaps causing a full on brawl from outside werewolf packs that are now fighting each other and the spirits, the werewolves thinking the PCs betrayed the now dead pack. It would be a cluster fuck of epic preportions. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5383-lonesomewanderer1982","name":"Lonesomewanderer1982","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T00:49:06-07:00","id":479995,"title":"","content":"There's two main things I want from as new edition. Someone earlier mentioned something similar to over if my points but I'll go over them again as it's not exactly the same. <br /> <br /> The first is making cross-group games easier conceptually and mechanically, within and across tiers (keep tiers in whatever sense you like - numerical, regional or whatever) . <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=169929#post169929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every Hunter group, cannon or fannon, falls into one of three modes:<br /> <br /> 1) We come from this background, and want to protect people from this background. (E.G. The Union, Task Force: VALKARIE, Ascending Ones)<br /> 2) We dislike and kill a certain kind of monster (E.G. MM, The Long Night, Division VI)<br /> 3) We can profit from hunting and killing a certain kind of monster (Cheiron, LDI, Utopia Now)</div> </div> </div> </div>If love to see groupings into 'super-conspiracies', that work thematically. Not exactly as King's Raven said, but at least collect up the government ones (VASCU and TFV) give the story teller options and ideas...is Cheiron Group employed by the government... Or is it the otherway round? Collect up the artifact users who stay mostly human (ascending ones, ADK etc ). Perhaps. Hopefully you get the picture. Perhaps have different groupings etc. <br /> <br /> Then give us how they *all* work together. How can a compact team up with a conspiracy? Give us game play examples of The union working with the ascending ones. Maybe TFV can't give Advanced Armoury to civilians but they can fund other equipment. I addition to this show us some compacts becoming conspiracies, and not just with the c&amp;c like endowments. <br /> <br /> Next point, tie profession into endowments. Maybe a TFV scientist can tweak his gear to improve some equipment bonuses. Maybe scientists in the Ascending Ones can craft their elixirs. Not every profession needs to alter their endowment, but some will, with professions leaning towards their natural conspiracy. <br /> <br /> That's all I have for now. On mobile so please forgive any spelling errors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T06:59:12-07:00","id":480171,"title":"","content":"One thing regarding lunacy: Since it now works as an integrity breaking point, theoretically a code could inure one to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}